{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical","id":1302901,"title":"How to explain technocrats not knowing , some of their effects are obviously magical?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-05T12:38:04-07:00","id":1302901,"title":"How to explain technocrats not knowing , some of their effects are obviously magical?","content":"I'm talking about the fact that their &quot;laser gun&quot; through which they channel forces 3 prime 2 laser bolts only works for them for some reason. And when a citizen uses it doesn't work.<br /> It's one thing to say that they are the only ones enlightened enough to do some super scientific complicates processes.. a laser gun , on the other side, only requires you to press a button.<br /> <br /> Up until now i've just handwaved the issue. Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T12:45:27-07:00","id":1302903,"title":"","content":"Disregarding rules somewhat; I'd give the Technos special gear. That way, they do have a special laser gun that'll work for anyone, just they can do more complicated stuff with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T13:04:27-07:00","id":1302906,"title":"","content":"... Technocrats know the effects aren't natural. The only ones who aren't in the loop are the unenlightened. If you can cast spells, you know full well you're mucking about with reality. The difference is one of philosophy and approach to that reality muckery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T13:16:33-07:00","id":1302910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical#post1302901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking about the fact that their &quot;laser gun&quot; through which they channel forces 3 prime 2 laser bolts only works for them for some reason. And when a citizen uses it doesn't work.<br /> It's one thing to say that they are the only ones enlightened enough to do some super scientific complicates processes.. a laser gun , on the other side, only requires you to press a button.<br /> <br /> Up until now i've just handwaved the issue. Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technocrats believe that they perform &quot;enlightened procedures&quot;. They know that there is a difference between awakened/enlightened people (Mages, essentially) and the masses. They know that there are things Black Suits can do that Extraordinary Citizens can't. They just explain it in ways that defy mysticism, occultism and &quot;magical&quot; legacies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T13:20:37-07:00","id":1302911,"title":"","content":"I think to answer your question, Technocrats don't believe in &quot;magic&quot;. They always have a way of rationalizing what they're doing as science, and their method of rationalizing is ultimately their paradigm.<br /> <br /> The laser gun you're referring to might just require a complex set of mechanisms to use, which other people just &quot;don't really get&quot;. Imagine that old radio that somehow only works for you, when you move the antenna juuuust right. Realistically, yes, some rando could potentially get it to work, but in game, they just won't. <br /> <br /> To Michael's point, it's on you/your GM to rationalize why you can use it and others can't. Usually saying &quot;it's a complex piece of machinery that you really need to understand to operate correctly&quot; is the go-to.<br /> <br /> Not that I'm an expert, but that's the way I understand it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24282-neveq","name":"Neveq","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T14:04:32-07:00","id":1302922,"title":"","content":"And even if the laser gun is actually simple to *use*, the Technocrats are aware that said laser gun<br /> <br /> 1) Would cause Paradox when seen<br /> 2) Paradox is caused by the Consensus (Heck, the Consensus was the Union's discovery)<br /> 3) Even if not a paradox-causing gadget: It still is essentially 'flying under the radar' of the consensus until it becomes a mundane everyday item<br /> 4) The Consensus is formed by sleepers<br /> <br /> Thus it would make sense for the laser gun, even if simple to use, not to work in the hands of a sleeper.<br /> Really, the Union *knows* its devices are special. They *know* about the Consensus and its mechanics.<br /> They simply consider &quot;Magic&quot; an uncontrolled, chaotic use of their Enlightened Principles, misguided through a lens of superstition and absurdity.<br /> They don't consider their enlightened principles to be magic - they consider everybody who uses 'magic' as abusing enlightened principles.<br /> They know all the things that the Traditions and others can do - they simply understand the cause and effect differently.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> And to add, to them the reason why an awakened mind can shoot fireballs from their hands, is because that mind is deranged, twisted, misguided, unhinged and way off the road of actual Enlightened Science.<br /> So, in a way, yes...Technocrats *do* believe they *could* shoot fireballs out of their hands.... if they'd turn into Enlightened Loonies.<br /> They do not believe a *sane* awakened/enlightened mind can do it. That is the key to unraveling the seeming paradox (pun not intended) of a Technocrat not believing they can do what Traditionalist Mages can do, while knowing they are in the same kind of awakened state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-14-2021, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T20:25:55-07:00","id":1302991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical#post1302901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking about the fact that their &quot;laser gun&quot; through which they channel forces 3 prime 2 laser bolts only works for them for some reason. And when a citizen uses it doesn't work.<br /> It's one thing to say that they are the only ones enlightened enough to do some super scientific complicates processes.. a laser gun , on the other side, only requires you to press a button.<br /> <br /> Up until now i've just handwaved the issue. Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel like everyone who makes this claim has NEEDS to work in Technical support for SIMPLE Things. &quot;How do I turn on my Computer&quot; is Something I have been asked repeatedly. &quot;I forgot how to save files&quot; is another one I've gotten recently. Or spending 20 minutes trying to walk someone through something that I started with &quot;activate the program that looks like a globe&quot; when they apparently were completely incapable of activating a program.<br /> <br /> So yeah is you present Laser guns as Less complex than a cellphone maybe its hard to do. IF you present them as having a certain amount of proprietary setup and cultural infrastructure that Every Technocrat sees as simple and the get upset that &quot;Sleepers&quot; just can't see the obviously simple interface.. or the Technocracy you know.. doesn't make the interface blindlingly &quot;Simple&quot; for outsiders because every idiot sleeper SHOULDN'T be using a laser gun. I am strongly doubting the Technocracy believes in Laser Gun Rights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T20:29:19-07:00","id":1302993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical#post1302901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking about the fact that their &quot;laser gun&quot; through which they channel forces 3 prime 2 laser bolts only works for them for some reason. And when a citizen uses it doesn't work.<br /> It's one thing to say that they are the only ones enlightened enough to do some super scientific complicates processes.. a laser gun , on the other side, only requires you to press a button.<br /> <br /> Up until now i've just handwaved the issue. Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me put a different spin on the question: let\u2019s say that you\u2019re working with a rules hack where the Technocracy\u2019s Enlightened Science <i>isn\u2019t</i> just Awakened Magick reskinned, but has known and quantifiable differences. We already have a bit of this in the rule that Technocrats don\u2019t get to surpass their Instruments <i>ever</i> and the rule that they don\u2019t have to expend Willpower or additional personal Quintessence in the creation of Devices or Principiae if using Technocratic facilities to construct them; but what if you\u2019re willing to bend the rules further? What would you do to make Enlightened Science perform as advertised, in particular on the matter of non-Enlightened personnel picking up an Instrument and attempting to use it? Would you ban Instruments and say that they can only work Enlightened Science through technological Wonders? Would you institute a house rule that a Sleeper <i>can</i> use Technocratic Instruments the way a Technocrat can? Would you impose a restriction that Instruments represent some sort of improvization (e.g., \u201cMcGuyvering\u201d) or access to hidden features in common utilities while Devices suffer no such restriction and can (theoretically) be used by anyone? Would you impose a formalized \u201cLearned Procedures\u201d system that requires practitioners of Enlightened Science to study and learn individual Procedures before they can perform them? <br /> <br /> I am contemplating just such a rules hack, and am looking for suggestions on what would work and what wouldn\u2019t; in particular, I\u2019m looking for advice on dealing with the \u201cif you\u2019re Enlightened, you can do this; if you\u2019re not, you can\u2019t\u201d dichotomy: when is it appropriate, and when isn\u2019t it appropriate? When it isn\u2019t appropriate, how do you address it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-05-2019, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T03:09:31-07:00","id":1303036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1302906#post1302906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Technocrats know the effects aren't natural. The only ones who aren't in the loop are the unenlightened. If you can cast spells, you know full well you're mucking about with reality. The difference is one of philosophy and approach to that reality muckery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. More than 90% of Awakened technocrats do not know this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T03:24:28-07:00","id":1303037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1303036#post1303036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. More than 90% of Awakened technocrats do not know this</div> </div> </div> </div>Er. Wrong, they know they are mucking about with reality. They *know* they are Enlightened.<br /> It was the Technocratic Union that even came up in-game with the term &quot;Consensus&quot; for the push of sleepers on reality, *not* the Traditions.<br /> <br /> I think what you are referring to is 90% of the Technocrats not literally thinking that what they do is actually 'Magic', but I refer to my post up higher in regards to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T03:54:21-07:00","id":1303041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1303037#post1303037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er. Wrong, they know they are mucking about with reality. They *know* they are Enlightened.<br /> It was the Technocratic Union that even came up in-game with the term &quot;Consensus&quot; for the push of sleepers on reality, *not* the Traditions.<br /> <br /> I think what you are referring to is 90% of the Technocrats not literally thinking that what they do is actually 'Magic', but I refer to my post up higher in regards to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The technocrats book explicitly says that they do not know they are altering reality. Other books back this up<br /> <br /> Edit: i do find it illogical, but it is still canon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T06:07:42-07:00","id":1303059,"title":"","content":"Part of interpreting Mage is keeping in mind that the writers aren't always on the same page. Don't hold too fast to canon if that canon is interfering with your understanding or enjoyment of the game. Look for alternate interpretations that work better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T10:22:59-07:00","id":1303111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1303041#post1303041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The technocrats book explicitly says that they do not know they are altering reality. Other books back this up<br /> <br /> Edit: i do find it illogical, but it is still canon</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. Because 90% of Technocrats aren't mages. The Enlightened portion of the Technocracy is not the majority of the organization.<br /> <br /> Anyone enlightened enough to use procedures knows what they're doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T11:54:38-07:00","id":1303145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1302922#post1302922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even if the laser gun is actually simple to *use*, the Technocrats are aware that said laser gun<br /> <br /> 1) Would cause Paradox when seen<br /> 2) Paradox is caused by the Consensus (Heck, the Consensus was the Union's discovery)<br /> 3) Even if not a paradox-causing gadget, still is essentially 'flying under the radar' of the consensus until it becomes a mundane everyday item<br /> 4) The Consensus is formed by sleepers<br /> <br /> Thus it would make sense for the laser gun, even if simple to use, not to work in the hands of a sleeper.<br /> Really, the Union *knows* its devices are special. They *know* about the Consensus and its mechanics.<br /> They simply consider &amp;quot;Magic&amp;quot; an uncontrolled, chaotic use of their Enlightened Principles, misguided through a lens of superstition and absurdity.<br /> They don't consider their enlightened principles to be magic - they consider everybody who uses 'magic' as abusing enlightened principles.<br /> They know all the things that the Traditions and others can do - they simply understand the cause and effect differently.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> And to add, to them the reason why an awakened mind can shoot fireballs from their hands, is because that mind is deranged, twisted, misguided, unhinged and way off the road of actual Enlightened Science.<br /> So, in a way, yes...Technocrats *do* believe they *could* shoot fireballs out of their hands.... if they'd turn into Enlightened Loonies.<br /> They do not believe a *sane* awakened/enlightened mind can do it. That is the key to unraveling the seeming paradox (pun not intended) of a Technocrat not believing they can do what Traditionalist Mages can do, while knowing they are in the same kind of awakened state.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked your theory, but does the books say that? That they think you must be crazy to be able to shoot fireballs?<br /> <br /> That's another thing i always wondered, how the technocrats explain mages casting spells just with their hands/voices/wands and why they don't tey to learn that, since it seems a lot more easier and independent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T12:27:54-07:00","id":1303155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1303041#post1303041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The technocrats book explicitly says that they do not know they are altering reality. Other books back this up<br /> <br /> Edit: i do find it illogical, but it is still canon</div> </div> </div> </div>The Union, at its heart, believes that reality needs a homogenous singular vision driving it forward, represented by the Timetable. A particularly philosophical White Suit might even, in a comfortable and intimate setting, admit that Technology is simply the convenient option since it has won out and is in control of mainstream reality. What matters is that you pick a single option, create conformity, and stick with it. If we were calling eachother with engraved mirrors and teleporting to work with special candles, there would be a Hermetic equivalent to the Technocracy trying to rewrite Reality to exclude other interpretations.<br /> <br /> Your average Black Suit might not fully appreciate this of course. Whether a Technocrat believes they are obeying the rules of reality, or setting the rules of reality, can actually depend. Regardless, they are certain that their way is RIGHT and that other ways are deviant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T12:36:26-07:00","id":1303157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1303145#post1303145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I liked your theory, but does the books say that? That they think you must be crazy to be able to shoot fireballs?<br /> <br /> That's another thing i always wondered, how the technocrats explain mages casting spells just with their hands/voices/wands and why they don't tey to learn that, since it seems a lot more easier and independent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shooting fireballs (outside of special exceptions like fireball-generating implanted tech, for example, and psionic pyrokinesis) is reality deviance. Every book (practically) underlines this idea that RDs are crazy or unmutual or not fit for existence.<br /> <br /> And the majority of Mages could have more convenient beliefs and practices. In fact, it would be very convenient for me to believe that charitable/kind acts were for suckers, and that the only morally righteous thing to do is follow a doctrine of Rational Self-Interest. But that's not what I believe, and I can't change it on a whim for the sake of convenience.<br /> <br /> Black Suit simply doesn't believe in &quot;magic&quot;, in a word. Hermetic Apprentice doesn't believe he can conjure fireballs with his smart phone. They'd both have an easier time, arguably, if they had technomystic/magi-technical beliefs which let them create fireballs using smart phones, but they don't believe that reality works like that. Even if they accept that other &quot;mages&quot; can perform magick that way (very likely for the Hermetic, who sees Virtual Adepts about their business, and potentially possible for the Black Suit who constantly witnesses Reality Deviance and might realize that he has the potential to do what they do), they simply won't because of their principled beliefs.<br /> <br /> It all comes back to Focus; Magick depends on it. And Focus = Paradigm + Practice + Instruments. The Black Suit is able to act as a Mage because his Might Makes Right Paradigm feeds neatly into his Martial Arts / Hypertech / Social Domination Practice, which he performs with Weapons, Vehicles, IDs and Warrants, Gadgets and Devices etc. etc. He's able to alter Reality because he believes in something very strongly. He can't flippantly decide to embrace something else because it's &quot;easy&quot;, especially while being a servant of the Technocratic Union, who reject many practices as unmutual.<br /> <br /> To almost the same extent this applies to our Hermetic. Sure, he could draw the Pentagram and Circles with a Graphics Pad, and do everything digitally, but he likes the way he does magick. It's what he's good at. If he took the time to develop Computer/Science to match his Occult/Esoterica/High Ritual, then the two might be equivalent. But he's heavily invested, both in terms of Dots on the sheet and concept, into the Hermetic Practice. It isn't a simple matter of him going &quot;well this would be easier in this day and age&quot;. Hermetics are proud; THIS DAY AND AGE IS WRONG. Magick still exists, and every time I do things MY WAY I prove that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T12:36:39-07:00","id":1303158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1303111#post1303111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's true. Because 90% of Technocrats aren't mages. The Enlightened portion of the Technocracy is not the majority of the organization.<br /> <br /> Anyone enlightened enough to use procedures knows what they're doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe other books explicitly state it is true even for enlightened members. Honestly you can tell just by reading the character profiles for various members &gt; lower ranking technocratic mages think as scientists, while the roleplaying hints on some higher ranking ones has them explicitly admit that they are mages<br /> <br /> It was even true back in the time of the order of reason, with the outer labyrinth not knowing that they are altering reality<br /> <br /> Edit: so, i just thought that maybe lower ranking(but enlightened) technocrats are conditioned(AKA social conditioning) to believe that their laser guns require special DNA clearance , or something like that. Dunno if it makes any sense. It does sound a little stupid to me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 04-06-2019, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T13:04:14-07:00","id":1303163,"title":"","content":"Let's step away from the notion that it's all the same thing for a moment, and consider it from the perspective of the Technocracy. In particular, let's take seriously their notion that Enlightened Science is something fundamentally different from Awakened Magick. <br /> <br /> It's not so much that you have to be crazy to work Magick as it is that you need a very different mindset from the one that the Enlightened have; it's one that's less about seeking truth than it is about imposing your will. As well, you need to engage a wild, untameable power, a fact that is amply demonstrated every time a Backlash occurs. Indeed, whatever it is that mages deal with seems at times to have a will of its own, and actively resists being constrained. This combination of willful mages and willful magick is a dangerous combination. Furthermore, it's only accessible to a rare few who have the Gift, whatever that is; this shuts most people, including most Technocrats, out. <br /> <br /> Enlightened Science is different. It's fundamentally about understanding, not ego; and what it harnesses are reliable if obscure forces of nature, not capricious powers with their own agendas. <br /> <br /> It's not that Technocrats don't believe that Magick exists (although I still contend that you can find a surprisingly high concentration of Negation Men \u2014 Denial-based Marauder variants whose disbelief tends to shut down Magick in their vicinity, reinforcing their disbelief and driving them further into Denial \u2014 in their ranks) as it is that they don't see it as a viable option <i>for them</i> (as most Technocrats, even the Enlightened ones, don't believe that they have whatever unique quality mages have that let them wield magick), and they look at those who <i>do</i> use it with distrust (but <i>not</i> envy; Enlightened Science has proven to be a match for Awakened Magick, and then some). <br /> <br /> There are technomancers who don't think this way, primarily among the Etherites (see the Scientific Mystic merit for what happens when you take the opposite view to its logical extreme); but it's an unpopular view, to say the least, in the Union.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T14:10:28-07:00","id":1303178,"title":"","content":"I agree that they could find logical explanations for the mystic effects, and that they might not be able to replicate them, since they mindset is quite opposite.<br /> <br /> But to not believe something that they often see is kinda illogical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T14:14:47-07:00","id":1303179,"title":"","content":"Yep. It's almost as if Technocrats who don't believe in something that they often see are in Denial\u2026<br /> <br /> Elaborating on this: I don\u2019t believe that there are all that many Technocrats who don\u2019t believe in Magick. I <i>do</i> think that there are enough of them that it\u2019s a problem (i.e., a significant minority), and that those who <i>do</i> deny the existence of Magick are all in a state of Denial to one extent or another; and the worst of these have crossed the line to being Negation Men. But the \u201ctypical\u201d Technocrat? \u201cYeah; Magick is real. And it\u2019s something different than what we do, and is inherently dangerous.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-22-2020, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T15:10:20-07:00","id":1303191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1303178#post1303178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that they could find logical explanations for the mystic effects, and that they might not be able to replicate them, since they mindset is quite opposite.<br /> <br /> But to not believe something that they often see is kinda illogical.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that they don't believe it is possible. It's that they believe it shouldn't be possible. That it's bad, that it's unscientific, that it harkens back to an age of darkness and primordialism where humans shat themselves to death because there was no sanitation and lived and died by random chance effecting crops.<br /> <br /> Technocrats are opposed to Reality Deviance because as a Union they've come up with a (mostly) coherent vision of Reality, and they reject anything that doesn't fall within that vision.<br /> <br /> Naturally these views get more sophisticated and nuanced as you go up the ranks, with the exceptions of Mages who are plagued by Denial Quiet. But the full gauntlet of &quot;this is possible, but outdated, and has no place in the modern world&quot; to &quot;yeah it's just reality deviance, don't think about it&quot; is present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T19:51:16-07:00","id":1303235,"title":"","content":"There are as many attitudes about why Superstitionists can do what they do, as there are Technocrats.<br /> <br /> One idea I like links directing to the idea of Intrinsic vs Extrinsic models of Magick. Specifically, that some Technocrats might believe both sides use their &quot;Enlightenment&quot; to change Reality. It's just that Technocrats have made a very specific value judgement about which is better (it's Extrinsic, obviously). To them, it matters what's &quot;doing the work&quot; behind an Effect, and what that method does to the Enlightened individual.<br /> <br /> Technocrats let their tools - whether a machine, institutional mechanics, or properly used (and modified) bodies - do all the work. All they have within their &quot;minds&quot; is understanding. The superstitionists, meanwhile, use their &quot;tools&quot; as simple props, to focus the true source of their power: their brains. Not their minds, their BRAINS. As far as some Technocrats are concerned, the mystics are just delusional psychics (just as the mystics are prone to believe that the psychics are delusional mystics). Save for a few Technocrats who employ psionics - a technique (Practice) that is heavily monitored - the Technocrats eschew this method.<br /> <br /> The reason, so the Technocrat would say, is because having the Mage's brain/mind do all the work has terrible side effects. On both a neurological and psychological level. The burden of superstitionist methods take their toll. Accepting strange and mutually contradictory models of reality. Modifying their brain chemistry with drugs, pain, stress, and periods of physical deprivation. Using such focus that they placebo their brains into growing aberrant glands on their cerebrum. (Even if they are too tiny to be noticed). Concentrating so much on deviant methods that it creates quirks in their psychology.<br /> <br /> All of this even before you get into how many superstitionists open their consciousnesses up to alien beings from other dimensions, which has who-knows-what negative effects on their psyche profiles.<br /> <br /> Combining these forces, it's no wonder their &quot;Procedures&quot; have a tendency to backfire (or backlash) on them, directly. The harm done to their bodies. The delusions and manias formed in their minds. Beings from other worlds or constructs of their subconscious being summoned to &quot;punish&quot; them (see also <i><a href=\"https://sfdebris.com/videos/films/forbiddenplanet.php\" target=\"_blank\">Forbidden Planet</a></i>). At least when a Technocrat's Enlightenment goes haywire, it usually affects their tools or the outside environment. At least, so the Technocrat says.<br /> <br /> To the Union, it's not so much that Deviants must be crazy to believe in mysticism. It's that believing in mysticism <i>MAKES</i> them crazy, over a long enough time period. Honestly, to the Union, capturing superstitionists and conditioning them to use only Enlightened Procedures is &quot;doing them a favor&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 07-22-2019, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T01:22:56-07:00","id":1303266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1303235#post1303235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One idea I like links directing to the idea of Intrinsic vs Extrinsic models of Magick. Specifically, that some Technocrats might believe both sides use their &quot;Enlightenment&quot; to change Reality. It's just that Technocrats have made a very specific value judgement about which is better (it's Extrinsic, obviously). To them, it matters what's &quot;doing the work&quot; behind an Effect, and what that method does to the Enlightened individual.<br /> <br /> Technocrats let their tools - whether a machine, institutional mechanics, or properly used (and modified) bodies - do all the work. All they have within their &quot;minds&quot; is understanding. The superstitionists, meanwhile, use their &quot;tools&quot; as simple props, to focus the true source of their power: their brains. Not their minds, their BRAINS. As far as some Technocrats are concerned, the mystics are just delusional psychics (just as the mystics are prone to believe that the psychics are delusional mystics). Save for a few Technocrats who employ psionics - a technique (Practice) that is heavily monitored - the Technocrats eschew this method.<br /> <br /> The reason, so the Technocrat would say, is because having the Mage's brain/mind do all the work has terrible side effects. On both a neurological and psychological level. The burden of superstitionist methods take their toll. Accepting strange and mutually contradictory models of reality. Modifying their brain chemistry with drugs, pain, stress, and periods of physical deprivation. <br /> <br /> All of this even before you get into how many superstitionists open their consciousnesses up to alien beings from other dimensions, which has who-knows-what negative effects on their psyche profiles.<br /> <br /> Combining these forces, it's no wonder their &quot;Procedures&quot; have a tendency to backfire (or backlash) on them, directly.<br /> <br /> To the Union, it's not so much that Deviants must be crazy to believe in mysticism. It's that believing in mysticism <i>MAKES</i> them crazy, over a long enough time period. Honestly, to the Union, capturing superstitionists and conditioning them to use only Enlightened Procedures is &quot;doing them a favor&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed with all of this.<br /> <br /> And if the Union wants to prove any of this, they just need to point to Marauders, and to Reality Deviants who behave in &quot;insane&quot; ways, anything from Nephandi to cultists. There are some merits to these beliefs; we have a word for separating your own beliefs from baseline reality to the point where it inconveniences and/or harms you. We call it mental illness.<br /> <br /> The Traditions are a collection of Psychics and Precursor Scientists (alchemy is messy pre-enlightenment chemistry, for example) who are slowly driving themselves insane. From the perspective of some Technocrats at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T02:01:04-07:00","id":1303268,"title":"","content":"That's not that far removed from how the Order of Reason conceptualised their magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1303163#post1303163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(although I still contend that you can find a surprisingly high concentration of Negation Men \u2014 Denial-based Marauder variants whose disbelief tends to shut down Magick in their vicinity, reinforcing their disbelief and driving them further into Denial \u2014 in their ranks</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that from the books or is that your idea? If the latter, that's really good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T02:28:35-07:00","id":1303273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1303268#post1303268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that from the books or is that your idea? If the latter, that's really good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Negation Men are in the books, if you mean that part. If you mean the idea of them being &quot;common&quot; in the Technocracy, then I'm not sure if the books ever imply or state that. I've thought it would be quite fitting in the past, since they're anti-magick given form almost, especially if their Denial didn't extend to standard Technocratic Procedures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T02:30:23-07:00","id":1303274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1303273#post1303273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Negation Men are in the books, if you mean that part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any idea where?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T03:44:01-07:00","id":1303277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1303274#post1303274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any idea where?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're in Book of Secrets, the systems for them are described under the parts about Marauders.<br /> <br /> The idea is that they have gone into such intense Denial Quiet that they have given up on the idea of Magick existing entirely, and they can no longer use their Spheres directly. Instead they just exude countermagick. They keep their Arete rating, and they use that to determine the range and intensity of their disbelief. This Arete rating can even increase, making them bigger forces of Reality's static nature.<br /> <br /> They're essentially anti-magick/counter-magick incarnate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T05:10:06-07:00","id":1303293,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Negation Men</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The maddest thing a mage can do is to deny the existence of magick. Even Technocrats \u2013 who suppress the very idea of magick \u2013 still enjoy the powers of Enlightened Science and hypertech control. Certain Marauders, however, negate the effects of magick because they refuse to believe it exists. Walking paradoxes, these Negation Men assert the strength of the Consensus through sheer deniability.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Not long ago, the idea of such Marauders would have been inconceivable; the Mad Ones, after all, assert Dynamism, not Stasis, and strive to bring humanity into some new, chaotic Mythic Age. But in the wake of the Week of Nightmares (or some other factor, if those events never occurred), certain mages went utterly mad with Denial: a form of insanity that refuses to admit the existence of otherwise obvious facts. Since then, the Negation Men (no one yet has met a Negation Woman, although they probably exist) lead apparently normal lives, suppressing magick whenever it occurs in their presence.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All Negation Men appear totally mundane. They have neither auras nor apparent souls, dress neatly, and share the fastidious habits of some folks with Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder. That disorder, in fact, seems to be part of their madness. On many levels, they appear to be perfect Technocratic drones \u2013 efficient, orderly, and controlled. The presence, however, of a Negation Man blunts Technocratic Science as well as mystic Arts; this, in turn, dampens Enlightened Devices and Procedures, many of which provide essential systems for Technocratic operations.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mages who\u2019ve begun to recognize the Negation Man Syndrome theorize that such Marauders began as Technocrats whose obsession with order became too strong. That might even be true. It\u2019s possible, however, that some Negation Men were mystic mages who broke under the strain of their Arts. In pushing those powers far from their conscious minds, these mages might have adopted that ultimate paradox: the wizard so Awakened that he denies his own Awakening.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In game terms, a Negation Man\u2019s Quiet is an extreme form of the Denial. Instead of using his Spheres to create magickal Effects, he uses them as a constant and unconscious form of Countermagick.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As an optional rule, a Negation Man\u2019s Arete Trait gets rolled against any magickal Effect within roughly 15 feet (four-and-a half meters/five yards) per point in his Arete. Each success removes one success from another mage\u2019s or Device\u2019s Effects. Despite his Awakening, a Negation Man also counts as a Sleeper witness whenever a mage of any kind performs magick in his presence. This requires no effort on the Negation Man\u2019s part; in place of the usual Marauder chaos, his madness manifests as crushing and unshakable normalcy. No matter what happens, such Mad Ones refuse to accept the possibility of magick. There can be female Negation Marauders; the syndrome simply asserts itself more frequently in men.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">George Blank</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">He doesn\u2019t actually use the name \u201cBlank.\u201d To everyone he meets, he\u2019s simply \u201cGeorge.\u201d Yet George has no aura, no apparent soul. His eyes seem a little too clear, his speech a bit too clipped for comfort. People who\u2019ve heard of Asperger\u2019s Syndrome wonder if George is a high-functioning Aspie. He\u2019s not, though \u2013 his apparent hyperfocus is instead a wide-eyed state of denial. George literally does not see extraordinary things. He\u2019s locked them out of his perceptions. To him, the world is orderly and correct, free from shadows and ambiguities. Like most Negation Men, he\u2019s polite and efficient \u2013 the good citizen of a technological world. To George, however, there\u2019s no sense of wonder or mystery in life, only the well-ordered function of a perfect universe\u2026 which, considering that he\u2019s a citizen in the World of Darkness, makes him seem crazy as a shithouse rat.<br /> <br /> (The above is from M20; personally I'm not a fan of the way aspergers is referred to here, I don't think anyone likes being called an &quot;aspie&quot;, but the overall concept is on-point)<br /> <br /> One thing M20 doesn't go into is whether Negation Men are strictly ALWAYS Witnesses, and ALWAYS cause Vulgarity. Does this apply to subtle Sensory Effects? Or Effects that suit the Marauder's Denial, like the ones that all citizens are happy with because of the Union's control? Can they still work for the Technocracy, or does their effect on Enlightened Procedures make this possible? Does the Union know about these people? What's their view of them?<br /> <br /> Personally, my view is that Negation Men should essentially take the form of The Consensus in Industrialized Reality, just exaggerated and made stronger. Anything that's Coincidental to Average Joe is Coincidental to Negation Man... well not quite. Negation Man is hyper-vigilant and extremely unforgiving. Regardless, he'll accept that sometimes the guy in the funny hat can pull rabbits out of his pockets; after all, that could just be a clever &quot;magic trick&quot;. He just won't buy &quot;coincidences&quot;, and conditional Coincidence won't work with him. If he's present at your Faith Healing session (not that he'd voluntarily attend), he's going to literally sour the mood and the magick.<br /> <br /> Negation Men can usually still work for the Union in a limited capacity, since most of the Union's procedures are Coincidental to him. They don't work well as Agents however, since to them an angry Werewolf is not an enemy to be defeated, but a delusion created by their own mind, or something they can't see at all. They're working desk jobs at the Union, they're guarding Union installations, they're present at critical junctures which would be targeted by Reality Deviants.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-07-2019, 08:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T08:57:03-07:00","id":1303330,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I use a slightly different version where the negation only applies to Effects that contradict the Negation Man's own Focus: if the Negation Man would consider the Effect to be Vulgar, <i>then</i> he brings the full weight of Denial down on it. And it's not that he can't do <i>any</i> Effects other than Countermagic so much as he can't do anything that's Vulgar. <br /> <br /> The version that shows up in <b>Book of Secrets</b> is what happens when the Negation Man's Focus is the same as the average Sleeper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T09:46:37-07:00","id":1303342,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it does seem like a concept with a bit more potential than it's allowed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T10:07:43-07:00","id":1303346,"title":"","content":"I just say that the average technocrat agent you will meet is a brainwashed tradition mage or orphan that has been kidnapped by an operative.<br /> <br /> During their mind altering process their belief are altered making them negation men that will only accept as a consensual some of the technocratic procedures.<br /> <br /> True enlightened citizitens of the technocrazy know that they are altering reality with Magick/Phychic powers but they put the charade of the mad genius surrounded by pseudo science and &quot;it\u00b4s a prototype&quot; in front of the negation men and the non enlighment personal for the sake of the consensus and fear of control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T11:09:45-07:00","id":1303364,"title":"","content":"\u2026and that's fine if you're okay with the Union being two-dimensional villains. Which, in terms of published material, didn't even make it as far as the Second Edition of the game: even as early as the Book of Shadows, we were getting ideas for a more nuanced Technocracy; and as of M20, they're presented as a potential protagonist faction on par with the Traditions and Disparates. <br /> <br /> If the Technocracy is a viable protagonist faction, the notion that everyone in it is either liars or dupes needs to die in a fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T12:55:03-07:00","id":1303386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1303364#post1303364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026and that's fine if you're okay with the Union being two-dimensional villains. Which, in terms of published material, didn't even make it as far as the Second Edition of the game: even as early as the Book of Shadows, we were getting ideas for a more nuanced Technocracy; and as of M20, they're presented as a potential protagonist faction on par with the Traditions and Disparates.<br /> <br /> If the Technocracy is a viable protagonist faction, the notion that everyone in it is either liars or dupes needs to die in a fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed with this. BUT the Union does have brainwashed/cloned/mind-controlled agents among its ranks. It's just not the majority. The Union has darker sides to it, and lighter sides to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T13:12:14-07:00","id":1303389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1303364#post1303364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026and that's fine if you're okay with the Union being two-dimensional villains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. You're confusing your preferences for what is actually possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T13:22:07-07:00","id":1303393,"title":"","content":"Oh? How so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T13:45:08-07:00","id":1303401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1303393#post1303393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh? How so?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's self-evidently wrong. I mean, you've read the 1e stuff, the individual Technocrats are not generally presented as two-dimensional people. The stories underlying the original convention books are all about individual members grappling and compromising with their place in the Technocracy, that's obvious material for games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T13:56:35-07:00","id":1303406,"title":"","content":"I think, then, that you misunderstood what I was saying; because I agree with your assessment of the original Convention Books, and see no conflict between that and what I said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T21:30:38-07:00","id":1303709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1303364#post1303364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026and that's fine if you're okay with the Union being two-dimensional villains. Which, in terms of published material, didn't even make it as far as the Second Edition of the game: even as early as the Book of Shadows, we were getting ideas for a more nuanced Technocracy; and as of M20, they're presented as a potential protagonist faction on par with the Traditions and Disparates.<br /> <br /> If the Technocracy is a viable protagonist faction, the notion that everyone in it is either liars or dupes needs to die in a fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think my comment has been greatly misunderstood<br /> <br /> Negation men may have been programeed but the more time fades the greater ability their ability to think for themselves and true non brainwashed technocrats who truly belive due themselves in the idea that the world is better with more vacines and less dragons exist and they are clearly referenced in my comment as knowing that they are doing magic/have pshycic power or a reality altering field but clearly are putting are putting the mad scientist charade for the sake of their ideal otherwise they wouldn\u00b4t call themselves enlightened personal.<br /> <br /> The best example of this are the characters of the guide of the technocrazy in their prologue , they know and say out of loud that they are sacrifizing their search of enlightement/ascension for their ideals and their belief is so strong that they don\u00b4t mind having to shoot a partner in the back to advance them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 04-09-2019, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T05:30:54-07:00","id":1303756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical#post1302901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking about the fact that their &quot;laser gun&quot; through which they channel forces 3 prime 2 laser bolts only works for them for some reason. And when a citizen uses it doesn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that there's a basic fault with this premise that ignores the rules (M20 for reference).<br /> <br /> Firstly if the 'laser gun' is a focus for a technocratic mage then there are many reasons it can't be used by a random citizen - they don't have the skills, training, aptitude, etc. This is extremely easy to hand wave, a mage's laser gun focus cannot be a mass produced item because there aren't any mass produced laser guns in the consensus. Such a focus item would have to be a one of a kind experimental model that needs constant adjustment, calibration, etc, etc to work - all of which is handwaved away by the rules simply giving you a bonus for a focus.<br /> <br /> Secondly if the laser gun is a weapon that a random citizen can use then it must be a Wonder of some kind and _can_ be used by the uninitiated.<br /> <br /> There isn't room in the rules for anything else so to ask a question about something that isn't allowed in the game design is kind of pointless.<br /> <br /> Lastly, a lot of Mage HAS to be handwaved using <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RuleOfCool\" target=\"_blank\">Rule of Cool</a> because there's a lot of 'enthusiastic' (aka BAD) writing in the game and concentrating on one minor point will just get you bent out of shape. you need to go with the flow not rage against every last little thing.<br /> <br /> The internet has a lot to answer for!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T09:29:15-07:00","id":1304222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1303756#post1303756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that there's a basic fault with this premise that ignores the rules (M20 for reference).<br /> <br /> Firstly if the 'laser gun' is a focus for a technocratic mage then there are many reasons it can't be used by a random citizen - they don't have the skills, training, aptitude, etc. This is extremely easy to hand wave, a mage's laser gun focus cannot be a mass produced item because there aren't any mass produced laser guns in the consensus. Such a focus item would have to be a one of a kind experimental model that needs constant adjustment, calibration, etc, etc to work - all of which is handwaved away by the rules simply giving you a bonus for a focus.<br /> <br /> Secondly if the laser gun is a weapon that a random citizen can use then it must be a Wonder of some kind and _can_ be used by the uninitiated.<br /> <br /> There isn't room in the rules for anything else so to ask a question about something that isn't allowed in the game design is kind of pointless.<br /> <br /> Lastly, a lot of Mage HAS to be handwaved using <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RuleOfCool\" target=\"_blank\">Rule of Cool</a> because there's a lot of 'enthusiastic' (aka BAD) writing in the game and concentrating on one minor point will just get you bent out of shape. you need to go with the flow not rage against every last little thing.<br /> <br /> The internet has a lot to answer for!</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, but even without adjustment,etc it should still be able to &quot;fire&quot; if someone presses the button, this is how weapons work. After all the average technocratic mage(although i can see that many people disagree about this) is not supposed to know that he is focusing his enlightened will. He is just Genius. Which makes sense with complex experiments but now with a freaking button.<br /> <br /> In the same way that , in real life, i can(crudely), use a police officer's gun, but building a nuke is entirely impossible for me. Even if you give me the meterials, the necessary equipment, the schematics , and a FAQ guide","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T10:08:13-07:00","id":1304226,"title":"","content":"Well, a narrative solution it's not to make Instrument ray-guns that can be opperated by pressing a button. If each time you shoot you need to calibrate the tachyon fluctuations using the Hidden Plank's Variable that relates matter, energy, and alternate dimensions, which is a variable that depends on the situation...then it's understandable that normal people can't use most of the time, in the same vein as you can't make a nuke. This would also explain why the gun does different things each time it's shoot.<br /> <br /> But, of course, rules and fluff don't say this is the way it should be done. And it IS an extra effort one needs to make in order to not know that what one does it's magick - I'm not defending Mage's choices here, merely providing a creative solution","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T10:55:21-07:00","id":1304251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1304226#post1304226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If each time you shoot you need to calibrate the tachyon fluctuations using the Hidden Plank's Variable that relates matter, energy, and alternate dimensions, which is a variable that depends on the situation...then it's understandable that normal people can't use most of the time, in the same vein as you can't make a nuke.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I would also give it a +3 difficulty to use in the heat of combat if it had to be fiddled with that much per shot &gt;_&gt;<br /> Which is, really, the reason I never quite can settle with that kind of explanation for the whole &quot;Why does the lasergun not work in the hands of a sleeper&quot; paradox (Lower p paradox). It would make a horrible thing to use even for the enligtened, in the cases it was seemingly made for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T11:03:11-07:00","id":1304259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1304251#post1304251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I would also give it a +3 difficulty to use in the heat of combat if it had to be fiddled with that much per shot &gt;_&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>What?, you can't calculate the Hidden Planck's Variable in two seconds flat, and then move the dial within the remaining second?, maybe you're not so much of a Genius after all...<br /> <br /> Personally, I think the +1 for Fast-Cast it's enough","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T11:06:36-07:00","id":1304264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1304259#post1304259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What?, you can't calculate the Hidden Planck's Variable in two seconds flat, and then move the dial within the remaining second?, maybe you're not so much of a Genius after all...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not without the Lightning Calculator merit I can't! D: DON'T JUDGE MEEEEE","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T11:47:28-07:00","id":1304276,"title":"","content":"Yeah; that explanation never really sat well with me, either. I tend to prefer the take that Technocrats specifically (and to a somewhat lesser extent, technomancers in general) make heavy use of Wonders, particularly Gadgets and Devices, and most of their gear falls into that category rather than Instruments for their Spheres. This is supported by the fact that Technocrats have a way around the Willpower point cost of creating a Device, and the fact that they're the only faction in the game with enough resources to justify the Requisitions Background. Indeed, if not for the needless nerfing of mortal protagonists in the game (e.g., not only do they lose out on getting Arete/Enlightenment and Spheres, but they're <i>also</i> short-changed in terms of Attributes, Abilities, and Backgrounds), one could arguably play a highly successful Technocratic agent who is an Extraordinary Citizen rather than an Enlightened Scientist. <br /> <br /> Which is not to say that Technocrats <i>don't</i> use Spheres; they do. But they generally don't use the Spheres <i>in the field</i>; and when they do, it should generally represent either some sort of McGuyvering or gadgeteering (i.e., cobbling together a gadget), or it should represent a <i>procedure</i>, with the central element being a process that they go through to get a desired result. That is, their Instruments aren't as important as <i>what they do with them.</i><br /> <br /> Another \u201chouse rule\u201d that I'd consider would be using the Spheres in a manner similar to <b>Adventure!</b>'s Dramatic Editing: the mechanics are the same as a mage casting a Coincidental Effect, but the justification for it is that the Technocrat is just lucky or competent (\u201cMagick Enhancing Abilities\u201d would be a big part of Technocratic Dramatic Editing, with various Coincidental Effects negating difficulty penalties with which the agent would otherwise have to contend). As with how it was described in <b>Adventure!</b> (as opposed to <b>Trinity Continuum</b>'s Talents, where it's described as subconscious probability manipulation), play it up as just a metagaming system to play up a genre convention, as opposed to being a measurable in-game phenomenon. This is also similar to how more recent games like Fate and Cortex Plus have narrative-driving game systems in them, without even a hint that expenditures of Fate Points or Plot Points represent any sort of in-game phenomenon.<br /> <br /> (I'd also allow an Enlightened Scientist with the Requisitions Background to use it as a \u201cSchroedinger's Wonder\u201d, using a minor variation on the above Dramatic Editing option to specify on the spot just what he requisitioned before heading out on the mission \u2014 the difference being that the Effect doesn't have to be Coincidental; instead, he makes his Enlightenment roll and, if he succeeds, retroactively assigns points from his Requisitions pool and whips out a Gadget or Device that in turn performs the desired Effect. He then has that gear for the remainder of the mission.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-11-2019, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T14:49:50-07:00","id":1304513,"title":"","content":"This perennial question seems to arise from the supposition that one could formulate a Procedure so simple that any dope could do it.<br /> <br /> Why would we assume this? The Guide to the Techs notes that, of course, rank-and-file citizens lack the education and insight to execute the scientific methods behind a Procedure properly. Why should we presume that this is stuff that any random grad student or bystander could understand, much less operate? There are rules for hypertech objects which are simple enough that a Genius is not required to operate them, and the process of their creation is difficult and expensive. Only repeated iterations of design are sufficient to simplify a device to the extent it works in Sleeping hands, and there's a whole subunit of a Convention devoted to getting that work done.<br /> <br /> In any case, a Technocrat <i>can </i>probablytell someone how to calibrate a laser rifle, hand it to them, and it will work - the mage rolls the Arete, the civilian handles the Instrument. With sufficient Data, you could do this remotely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T14:59:43-07:00","id":1304516,"title":"","content":"Indeed \u2014 although this requires that there be more to the Procedure than \u201cpoint and click\u201d \u2014 which in turn means that the standard example of using a raygun probably isn't a good example of a Procedure. <br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> like your example of an Enlightened Scientist walking someone through a Procedure and performing it by proxy. I'm not sure how valid that is under a strict reading of the rules (it's comparable to making and using a single Gadget on the spot, and might arguably require a couple dots of Primal Utility); but even if it's not strictly valid, it's a reasonable enough house rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T17:14:41-07:00","id":1304539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1304516#post1304516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed \u2014 although this requires that there be more to the Procedure than \u201cpoint and click\u201d \u2014 which in turn means that the standard example of using a raygun probably isn't a good example of a Procedure.<br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> like your example of an Enlightened Scientist walking someone through a Procedure and performing it by proxy. I'm not sure how valid that is under a strict reading of the rules (it's comparable to making and using a single Gadget on the spot, and might arguably require a couple dots of Primal Utility); but even if it's not strictly valid, it's a reasonable enough house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd let that fall under the &quot;Targets&quot; rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T04:34:00-07:00","id":1304780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1304516#post1304516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed \u2014 although this requires that there be more to the Procedure than \u201cpoint and click\u201d \u2014 which in turn means that the standard example of using a raygun probably isn't a good example of a Procedure.<br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> like your example of an Enlightened Scientist walking someone through a Procedure and performing it by proxy. I'm not sure how valid that is under a strict reading of the rules (it's comparable to making and using a single Gadget on the spot, and might arguably require a couple dots of Primal Utility); but even if it's not strictly valid, it's a reasonable enough house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simplicity itself: the Mage has &quot;Human Resources&quot; as one of their Instruments. They are skilled in the art of guiding subordinates or allies into carrying out the Mage's Will. In essence, the Extraordinary Citizen is simply a living, breathing tool for Enlightened Science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T09:22:11-07:00","id":1304821,"title":"","content":"I am genuinely confused that anyone who read the foundations of the Technocracy could come to the conclusion that they're unaware that they're performing magic. It's outright stated in the first precept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Order, Stasis, and Consensus<br /> Bring Stasis and order to the Universe. Predictability brings safety. Once all is discovered and all is known, Unity will be won. <br /> <br /> Magick, by its very nature, is unpredictable and capricious. Elite Technocrats work with experimental and unpredictable technology, but their ultimate goal is to standardize that tech. Their futuristic innovations are tested and iterated until those inventions become safe and predictable tools that can benefit humanity. Think of the Technocrats, if you will, as the ultimate alpha testers \u2013 the earliest of early adopters.Instead of \u201cspells,\u201d \u201ctalismans\u201d and \u201crituals,\u201d Technocrats develop Procedures, Adjustments, Devices, and Processes, training their operatives to minimize the inherent risks of Enlightened Science. Although vulgar willworking is possible (using what agents call blatant Procedures), it\u2019s actively discouraged. Coincidental willworking (or as agents call it, subtle Procedures) is far more predictable, largely because it almost always appears as advanced technology or scientific applications. This way, the impossible becomes commonplace and predictable. Instead of a world of supernatural horror and endless mystery, the Union tames a world in which everything can be defined, classified, quantified, and ultimately controlled.Thanks to Anthropic Field Theory (a Technocratic explanation for the effects of human beliefs upon reality), human consciousness directs the flow of Earthly phenomena. Technocrats do not program that flow so much as they direct it along the most desirable outcomes for humanity at large. Thus, although a technological elite leads the Technocracy, many agents believe that their Union fights for a world in which reality is shaped by the common populace \u2013 by the Masses, not by an anachronistic alliance of mages. The world these agents create is the world that humanity wants \u2013 in Technocratic terminology, the Consensus, the ultimate manifestation of the Anthropic Field Theory. Eventually, the Masses will get to share the same advanced technology that the Technocracy employs. Once the Union\u2019s power becomes fully invested and integrated into human discourse and its Consensus, such radical measures will no longer be experimental. They will be predictable. They will be controlled. In short, they will be the very opposite of magick. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T11:25:42-07:00","id":1304847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PazuzuAxelf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1304821#post1304821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am genuinely confused that anyone who read the foundations of the Technocracy could come to the conclusion that they're unaware that they're performing magic. It's outright stated in the first precept.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This section is written from an OOC perspective; Technocrats (in general) don't think what they're doing is magical in any way, shape or form. The more senior you get, the closer and closer the explanation gets to basically being a description of magic, BUT what's important is that even if a White Suit has an understanding of procedures / enlightened technology that sounds functionally identical to magic, they'd never use that word. At the most absurd extreme (which is intentional on the part of the writers, MtA has satirical elements, most notably the way everyone is using the same system but would never see/admit that) you have technocrats almost saying something akin to &quot;oh this isn't SALT, this is Sodium Chloride&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T13:14:31-07:00","id":1304867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical#post1302901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking about the fact that their &quot;laser gun&quot; through which they channel forces 3 prime 2 laser bolts only works for them for some reason. And when a citizen uses it doesn't work.<br /> It's one thing to say that they are the only ones enlightened enough to do some super scientific complicates processes.. a laser gun , on the other side, only requires you to press a button.<br /> <br /> Up until now i've just handwaved the issue. Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>A laser gun is probably going to be a device rather than a focus. At least that is my guess. (I suppose one might also make the argument that, in the World of Darkness, the average 1st world urban &quot;citizen&quot; has been conditioned by NWO propoganda to believe that all guns are dangerous and should/can only be used by trained agents of authority, or perhaps that such a high tech weapon has either a complicated safety switch or handprint scanner that only allows &quot;the right people&quot; to use it.) <br /> <br /> As for the larger question of the thread title:<br /> <br /> <b>Doublethink</b> - <i>The power of holding two contradictory beliefs in one's mind simultaneously and accepting both of them.</i><br /> <br /> It's part of the newspeak from Orwell's Nineteen Eighty-Four. For someone to notice - let alone point out - any of the inherent contradictions in the official positions of Oceania's ruling Party was an act of crimethink punishable by instant social disapproval or even ostracism from one's peers and likely disiplinary action. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">To know and not to know, to be conscious of complete truthfulness while telling carefully constructed lies, to hold simultaneously two opinions which cancelled out, knowing them to be contradictory and believing in both of them, to use logic against logic, to repudiate morality while laying claim to it, to believe that democracy was impossible and that the Party was the guardian of democracy, to forget whatever it was necessary to forget, then to draw it back into memory again at the moment when it was needed, and then promptly to forget it again, and above all, to apply the same process to the process itself\u2014that was the ultimate subtlety: consciously to induce unconsciousness, and then, once again, to become unconscious of the act of hypnosis you had just performed. Even to understand the word\u2014doublethink\u2014involved the use of doublethink.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A properly trained Technocrat embraces doublethink to the point that they bellyfeel blackwhite.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T13:37:38-07:00","id":1304871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PazuzuAxelf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1304821#post1304821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am genuinely confused that anyone who read the foundations of the Technocracy could come to the conclusion that they're unaware that they're performing magic. It's outright stated in the first precept.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Note how the quoted section essentially says \u201cmagick is inherently unpredictable and capricious; what the Technocracy does is only risky when it's experimental.\u201d The whole section delineates between Magick and Enlightened Science, putting forth the notion that there are fundamental differences between them. <br /> <br /> There's also the question of how widespread the Anthropic Field Theory is among the Conventions. You won't find it in any Mage book prior to M20, save only for the Revised Void Engineers Convention Book where it was introduced. That said, the NWO has been the main proponents in the Union that belief shapes reality and that if you can control the Masses, you can control everything. I would say that Anthropic Field Theory is widespread in those two Conventions and not so much among the Syndicate, Iteration X, and the Progenitors. <br /> <br /> I would also point out that the Enlightened Anthropic Principle, as outlined in the aforementioned Convention Book, does not posit that Reality is subjective; it does state that there are fundamental laws of Reality that exist independent of human belief. Where it gets dangerously close to the Traditions' view of a subjective Reality is that it admits that Reality is <i>influenced by</i> human belief. <br /> <br /> That said, in my games another part of that theory is an Enlightened version of some interpretations of Quantum Mechanics, specifically \u201cwave Function collapse\u201d interpretations: \u201cwhat is possible\u201d is constrained by \u201cwhat is\u201d; it's only when \u201cwhat is\u201d is in doubt that there can be a Wave Function to collapse. And it's only when there's a Wave Function to collapse that whatever humans can do factors in. As for what that is, the Traditions say that it's a matter of Will, forcing Reality to conform to your beliefs; what the Conventions contend is that it's a matter of Observation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-06-2020, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T16:03:38-07:00","id":1304903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1304780#post1304780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simplicity itself: the Mage has &quot;Human Resources&quot; as one of their Instruments. They are skilled in the art of guiding subordinates or allies into carrying out the Mage's Will. In essence, the Extraordinary Citizen is simply a living, breathing tool for Enlightened Science.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is.. just genius and maybe something I wouldn't limit to technocrats..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T16:29:12-07:00","id":1304911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1304903#post1304903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is.. just genius and maybe something I wouldn't limit to technocrats..</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah Management &amp; HR is a really great tool, and it starts to blur the line between Sphere Effects and Static Reality sometimes. For example, an Ecstatic with a huge entourage could employ her Cult/Retainers/Allies/Backup Backgrounds (groupies, stylists, personal assistants, therapists) before a gig, making them a Management instrument for a series of effects that help her perform perfectly during the show, temporarily elevating her Attributes and reducing difficulties. But this is so incredibly coincidental that it borders on being &quot;so logical and real it's not magick&quot;. But there's actually something cool about that; coincidental effects so subtle that no one would notice them at all.<br /> <br /> In fact, Celebrities probably make a lot of weird things seem normal. If an idol has a pet fox, practices crystal therapy, says she's a &quot;pop priestess&quot; with psychic powers... I mean she's probably still among the more normal singers in the lineup. And that could help swing some things as coincidental! With Fame 4, talking about Past Life Regression in your interviews will attract some negative attention (scrutiny from the NWO for example), but Hollywood is full of people who publicly practice mysticism; just look how popular Kabbalah is among stars as one example.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh she just has her weird little rituals, all her staff humour her since it boosts her confidence.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-14-2019, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T19:51:20-07:00","id":1304957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1304903#post1304903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is.. just genius and maybe something I wouldn't limit to technocrats..</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, I was considering saying &quot;...a living, breathing tool for Enlightened Science <i>(or Awakened Magick)</i>&quot;. But at the time of the post, I was super tired and couldn't muster the energy. So I just sent it through as is.<br /> <br /> To be clear, &quot;Human Resources&quot; is hardly an Instrument limited to Technocrats. &quot;Group Rites&quot; are also an Instrument, and any mystic would tell you the benefits of getting a number of Acolytes, Cultists, and fellow Mages together for a good ol' High Ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T20:25:44-07:00","id":1304966,"title":"","content":"I am thinking like the Enlightened Tactician now. He calls out commands and his guys do that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T20:44:46-07:00","id":1304971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1304966#post1304966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am thinking like the Enlightened Tactician now. He calls out commands and his guys do that...</div> </div> </div> </div>1) One that sits at a terminal, watching teams on a series of screens and issuing orders.<br /> <br /> 2) An Enlightened tactical officer that leads SWAT-like strike teams of Extraordinary Citizens, using spoken commands, gadgets, and hand signs to direct their squad toward victory.<br /> <br /> 3) An Iteration X agent who oversees teams of technicians in pulling off huge engineering projects, not unlike their predecessors the Craftmasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T20:48:24-07:00","id":1304972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1304971#post1304971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) One that sits at a terminal, watching teams on a series of screens and issuing orders.<br /> <br /> 2) An Enlightened tactical officer that leads SWAT-like strike teams of Extraordinary Citizens, using spoken commands, gadgets, and hand signs to direct their squad toward victory.<br /> <br /> 3) An Iteration X agent who oversees teams of technicians in pulling off huge engineering projects, not unlike their predecessors the Craftmasons.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 4) a Void Engineer Space Marine officer who leads his troops into the front for the good of the world.<br /> <br /> 5) A super solider who's superior charisma and tactical accumen allows those under his command to rise up in ways they never thought possible..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T21:36:34-07:00","id":1304986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1304780#post1304780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simplicity itself: the Mage has &quot;Human Resources&quot; as one of their Instruments. They are skilled in the art of guiding subordinates or allies into carrying out the Mage's Will. In essence, the Extraordinary Citizen is simply a living, breathing tool for Enlightened Science.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to say that somewhere - Guide to the Technocracy, maybe, or the Book of Mirrors or one of the Sorcerers' Crusade books? - there was mention of Technocrats being able to train unAwakened underlings to perform specific rotes/procedures by operating the proper tools. I wish I could remember the specifics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T23:49:45-07:00","id":1305000,"title":"","content":"All that is well and good. But the real beauty of the earlier suggestion is that it at least partly answers the question of \u201cwhy can't Sleepers perform Technocratic Procedures?\u201d They <i>can</i>; but only if they're guided through the Procedure by someone who knows what he's doing (e.g., an Enlightened Scientist). <br /> <br /> Then you get the follow-up question, \u201cwhy can't Sleepers learn to perform the Procedure on their own?\u201d That can also be addressed with existing rules, though not as gracefully: they <i>can</i> \u201clearn\u201d the Procedure, if the Procedure is turned into a Virtual Wonder and given to them. Think of it like <i>The Matrix</i>'s \u201cI know Kung Fu\u201d: it's a way of inserting capabilities (in this case, Procedures) directly into someone's mind. The catch is that, per the rules as written, each instance of such a Wonder requires an investment of Quintessence; and it's implanted, not learned. Which is why I apply a fairly simple house rule: a teacher can gradually craft a Virtual Wonder in a student's mind without having to incorporate any Quintessence into it \u2014 <i>if</i> the student puts the appropriate effort into learning it and expends an appropriate amount of XP in lieu of the usual Quintessence cost. <br /> <br /> Et voila! A (nearly) rules-as-written means of addressing the most common critique about Technocrats not knowing that what they do is, in fact, Magick: their Procedures <i>can</i> be taught to and performed by individuals who are willing to put in the effort to learn, whether or not they're Enlightened \u2014 provided they have a qualified instructor; just like their Devices can be picked up and used by people who don't abuse them (read: Extraordinary Citizens: Sleepers with a sufficiently Technocratic Focus).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T05:16:16-07:00","id":1305020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1305000#post1305000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that is well and good. But the real beauty of the earlier suggestion is that it at least partly answers the question of \u201cwhy can't Sleepers perform Technocratic Procedures?\u201d They <i>can</i>; but only if they're guided through the Procedure by someone who knows what he's doing (e.g., an Enlightened Scientist).<br /> <br /> Then you get the follow-up question, \u201cwhy can't Sleepers learn to perform the Procedure on their own?\u201d That can also be addressed with existing rules, though not as gracefully: they <i>can</i> \u201clearn\u201d the Procedure, if the Procedure is turned into a Virtual Wonder and given to them. Think of it like <i>The Matrix</i>'s \u201cI know Kung Fu\u201d: it's a way of inserting capabilities (in this case, Procedures) directly into someone's mind. The catch is that, per the rules as written, each instance of such a Wonder requires an investment of Quintessence; and it's implanted, not learned. Which is why I apply a fairly simple house rule: a teacher can gradually craft a Virtual Wonder in a student's mind without having to incorporate any Quintessence into it \u2014 <i>if</i> the student puts the appropriate effort into learning it and expends an appropriate amount of XP in lieu of the usual Quintessence cost.<br /> <br /> Et voila! A (nearly) rules-as-written means of addressing the most common critique about Technocrats not knowing that what they do is, in fact, Magick: their Procedures <i>can</i> be taught to and performed by individuals who are willing to put in the effort to learn, whether or not they're Enlightened \u2014 provided they have a qualified instructor; just like their Devices can be picked up and used by people who don't abuse them (read: Extraordinary Citizens: Sleepers with a sufficiently Technocratic Focus).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Would you only allow this for Technocrats because it seems like it fixes the issue of the with teaching &quot;Sorcery&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T07:28:18-07:00","id":1305040,"title":"","content":"No, I wouldn't limit it to the Technocracy. That said, crafting a Talisman (which is what is needed to allow a Sleeper to \u201clearn\u201d a Rote) requires the investment of a permanent point of Willpower. This limits its usefulness when teaching \u201cacolyte magick\u201d unless you can offload the Willpower cost onto the student as well (possibly in the form of, say, an 8-xp surcharge on learning the Rote). Note that, under the right circumstances (i.e., when using proper facilities), the Technocracy gets to waive that Willpower cost, making it a more useful option for them. But yes, it did occur to me that this could be used to provide a Sphere Magick substitute for Sorcery.<br /> <br /> I go into more depth on this in my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1263470-spellbooks\">Spellbooks</a> hack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-15-2019, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T08:19:03-07:00","id":1305058,"title":"","content":"One effect listed in an M20 book is a Syndicate rep using the Management/HR instrument as part of the focus of an effect where he acquires a cab... and as fitting/natural as that is (make it an Entropy, Correspondence or Time effect, or all of the above, to get the taxi as soon as possible), &quot;I send a PA to grab me a cab while I wrap up the meeting&quot; is... so mundane. So normal. But there's something to like about that, Mages with ultra-coincidental effects/procedures.<br /> <br /> It could even apply in combat; shouting orders and encouragement at your bodyguards to trigger certain effects. Taking it step by step, as an example;<br /> <br /> What is the CHARACTER trying to do? - playing with the idea of awakened will empowering other minds/bodies, she's attempting to get her bodyguards to &quot;kick ass&quot; more effectively using her orders as a focus.<br /> <br /> What is the player doing? - a (Time 3 for extra actions, Prime 2 for aggravated damage, Life 3 for extra Strength, various Level 1 Sphere effects for reduced difficulty etc. etc.) effect using the Management and Voices/Vocalizations instruments, under the Social Domination practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T08:55:14-07:00","id":1305067,"title":"","content":"And for those that don't have Human Resources as an Instrument, it may still be doable under the &quot;working with unfamiliar tools&quot; rule.<br /> <br /> How to RP this? : The Etherite knowing how to calibrate the ray gun doesn't mean she knows how to explain the process of calibration very well. She can still try, but for a misantropist like her it will be harder (+2 penalty for unfamiliar tool). If she wants to lend her raygun in the future, learning Mad Pedagogy to better teach the correct equations would do wonders (maybe even Wonders)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T09:06:06-07:00","id":1305069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1305067#post1305067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And for those that don't have Human Resources as an Instrument, it may still be doable under the &quot;working with unfamiliar tools&quot; rule.<br /> <br /> How to RP this? : The Etherite knowing how to calibrate the ray gun doesn't mean she knows how to explain the process of calibration very well. She can still try, but for a misantropist like her it will be harder (+2 penalty for unfamiliar tool). If she wants to lend her raygun in the future, learning Mad Pedagogy to better teach the correct equations would do wonders (maybe even Wonders)</div> </div> </div> </div>And it's important to remember, from an OOC perspective, that the person who is calibrating and firing the weapon is being given that ability via the enlightened will of the Etherite. They are simply part of the instrument. Furthermore, unless you're using Correspondence you'll need to be present, and unless you're using Time it will need to be done within the Scene and not later on. It's also going to be roll for roll; if you want to give someone the ability to use these powers long term then you're going to be handing them a Wonder or making them into a Wonder, or trying to use magick to help them Awaken, or trying to teach them Sorcery, and all of those are quite complicated (especially the last two, since triggering Awakening is not easy/simple, and Mages aren't that great at teaching people static magic since they don't actually use it).<br /> <br /> IC explanations of this could be quite meta &quot;only with the oversight of my enlightened scientific paradigm can a regular sleeper like yourself perform such procedures&quot; or more obvious &quot;well you obviously got it wrong, these procedures are incredibly complex and I shouldn't have assumed you'd be able to do it without direct oversight&quot;.<br /> <br /> But this sort of tool does give stay-at-home VAs more power; imagine a character... you know that Guy in the Show who stays at base and looks at the computer screens and tells people &quot;what the hell they're looking at&quot;? Your Chloes (24), your Arams (Blacklist). Well using Data such a character can perform effects from afar, via other people, using Management and Telecommunications instruments. All that matters is that they believe they can perform the effect; helping their agent at the scene blow a circuit to cause an explosion? Awesome, use Forces 2-4 and Data 2-4, possibly with some Prime. Making the agent create electricity out of thin air to throw at people? I mean MAYBE. Some VAs have technomagickal beliefs (the techgnosi merit covers this), but this is going to be a Vulgar / Working Without Usual Tools situation in most cases, making it much harder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-15-2019, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T02:17:02-07:00","id":1322911,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve just been reading several of the technocracy books, most notably convention book $yndicate, and it makes it quite clear that the technocrats know they are forcing their will on reality, just as tradition mages do. Convention mages know they are fighting an ascension war. They know they have to be careful about paradox. Remember that the NWO is all about controlling the message, and the $yndicate loves to control the messengers. The terms that the technocracy uses are tools in their ascension war and shouldn\u2019t be seen as strictly indicative of what the conventions actually believe. The recognition of this fact is why the convention book: $yndicate specifically calls out the \u201cwar of words\u201d in which the $yndicate acknowledges the term \u201cparadox\u201d, but says they prefer the term \u201cMarket Correction\u201d while the NWO and ItX call the same phenomenon \u201cstatistical inevitability\u201d.. they then suggest that in mixed company a person should just say \u201cparadox\u201d. They see this war of words as an actual conflict with the NWO.<br /> However, there are also reasons why the unenlightened wouldn\u2019t be able to use technocrat items.. allowing them to do so would be dangerous. Certainly a MIB\u2019s gun would be gene-locked or SMART-fire or something like that.. some people of these safety features might be overcome if the technocrat has time to explain it to the user. Also, there are some items,like the MIDAS card, that are specifically designed so the unenlightened can use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T06:28:43-07:00","id":1322949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gothik_Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1322911#post1322911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve just been reading several of the technocracy books, most notably convention book $yndicate, and it makes it quite clear that the technocrats know they are forcing their will on reality, just as tradition mages do. Convention mages know they are fighting an ascension war. They know they have to be careful about paradox. Remember that the NWO is all about controlling the message, and the $yndicate loves to control the messengers. The terms that the technocracy uses are tools in their ascension war and shouldn\u2019t be seen as strictly indicative of what the conventions actually believe. The recognition of this fact is why the convention book: $yndicate specifically calls out the \u201cwar of words\u201d in which the $yndicate acknowledges the term \u201cparadox\u201d, but says they prefer the term \u201cMarket Correction\u201d while the NWO and ItX call the same phenomenon \u201cstatistical inevitability\u201d.. they then suggest that in mixed company a person should just say \u201cparadox\u201d. They see this war of words as an actual conflict with the NWO.<br /> However, there are also reasons why the unenlightened wouldn\u2019t be able to use technocrat items.. allowing them to do so would be dangerous. Certainly a MIB\u2019s gun would be gene-locked or SMART-fire or something like that.. some people of these safety features might be overcome if the technocrat has time to explain it to the user. Also, there are some items,like the MIDAS card, that are specifically designed so the unenlightened can use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case it's a retcon. Cause guide to the technocracy explicitly says that most awakened members don't know that they are mages. The book about the order of reason says the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T09:09:24-07:00","id":1322980,"title":"","content":"The unawakened Extraordinary Citizens, which often are technomancer sorcerers, are the ones who don't realize they're performing magic. The awakened nearly always do know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T10:37:27-07:00","id":1322988,"title":"","content":"it's just an edition thing,<br /> guide to the technocracy was 2nd ed,<br /> only the arch-technos knew they were doing magic<br /> <br /> in revised, things changed,<br /> the arch-technos died, and the regular techies learned the truth somehow<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T10:46:22-07:00","id":1322990,"title":"","content":"It all depends on what you mean by \u201cdoing magic\u201d. See my earlier posts in this thread on the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T11:44:18-07:00","id":1323008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1322988#post1322988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's just an edition thing,<br /> guide to the technocracy was 2nd ed,<br /> only the arch-technos knew they were doing magic<br /> <br /> in revised, things changed,<br /> the arch-technos died, and the regular techies learned the truth somehow</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that corrupting elements, highly placed in the Union, were specifically trying to destroy Magic in an attempt to weaken the world\u2019s defenses in preparation for an upcoming demonic invasion. As I mentioned before, words have power in the technocracy and I can see a rote in which corrupting technocrats could have others start buying into their own propaganda. When the corrupting factors are removed.. or at least weakened, uncorrupted technocrats would start thinking more like themselves. Admittedly, that\u2019s speculation on my part. I\u2019m not aware of any place where the books actually present that idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T14:20:18-07:00","id":1323049,"title":"","content":"that's actually an interesting theory","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T14:34:00-07:00","id":1323055,"title":"","content":"Well, M20 has confirmed the existence of the \u201cTechnephandi\u201d, so there could be something to that idea. That said, it's still based on the idea that all Technocrats are either liars or dupes; so while I would allow some of that to be going on in my games, I would <i>not</i> use it as <i>the</i> explanation for Technocrats not believing that what they do is magic. I'll stick to the more nuanced idea that the Technocracy has an alternative to the Purple Paradigm that hey embrace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-17-2020, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T19:59:04-07:00","id":1323113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1322949#post1322949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case it's a retcon. Cause guide to the technocracy explicitly says that most awakened members don't know that they are mages. The book about the order of reason says the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guide to the Technocracy says nothing of the sort. It says they don't believe they are mages and then explains why there is a difference between what they do and what mages do. It's an Ideological difference. Not a practical one. They know they warp reality. They just think they do it responsibily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T20:05:16-07:00","id":1323114,"title":"","content":"Warp reality, exploit loopholes in reality; toMAYto, toMAHto.<br /> <br /> M20 has a line in the section about Reality Zones along the lines that the Technocracy is very much aware of Earthly Foundations and takes pride in building on said Foundations rather than just doing whatever they like \u2014 that being a principle difference in their perspective and the Traditions' perspectives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-08-2019, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T01:03:28-07:00","id":1323391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1323055#post1323055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, M20 has confirmed the existence of the \u201cTechnephandi\u201d, so there could be something to that idea. That said, it's still based on the idea that all Technocrats are either liars or dupes; so while I would allow some of that too be going on in my games, I would <i>not</i> use it as <i>the</i> explanation for Technocrats not believing that what they do is magic. I'll stick to the more nuanced idea that the Technocracy has an alternative to the Purple Paradigm that hey embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the nephandi were taking over the technocracy. The part I can\u2019t really prove is the idea of a mass rote causing technocrats to buy into their own propaganda. Also, while it seems like losing most of their top echelons helped purge the technocracy, I can\u2019t exactly prove that either.<br /> <br /> Also, the technocracy aren\u2019t \u201cliars and dupes\u201d.. if you were to ask the N.W.O. they would probably tell you they are \u201cpeople who tell more believable variations on the truth and team players.\u201d<br /> <br /> The point being that lying and \u201cbeing dupes\u201d isn\u2019t just some side effect of being in the technocracy. N.W.O. magic is literally based on controlling messages and and following orders.. that\u2019s their paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23753,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","user":"Gothik_Knight","date":". 07-10-2019, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T10:48:39-07:00","id":1323469,"title":"","content":"It's \u201cliars <i>or</i> dupes\u201d, and is my shorthand for \u201cevery Technocrats either knows that they're altering reality and is lying about it (the liars), or they think that they aren't because their superiors are lying to them (the dupes)\u201d. Saying that the whole thing is just propaganda but they seem to have bought into their own propaganda is very much a \u201cliars or dupes\u201d argument. To be clear, my main objection to the \u201cliars or dupes\u201d line of argument has nothing to do with how believable it may or may not be; it's entirely about the viability of the Union as protagonists in the game. To my mind, that's hard to do if they're either fundamentally mistaken about the nature of reality or are lying about it. <br /> <br /> That's why my own preference is to say that <i>they have a valid point</i>. They're not deceiving or being deceived as to the underlying nature of reality; they just see it differently than the Traditions do. <i>And</i> their view as to the fundamentals of reality holds up about as well as the Traditions' collective view does \u2014 which is to say that it's not perfect, but it addresses some issues that the opposing view doesn't. In particular, overly simplistic versions of both views exist, and agents and mages on both sides who buy into these overly simplistic models are wrong, while agents and mages on both sides who push these overly simplistic models are being deceptive. <br /> <br /> It's still true that Conditioning exists \u2014 though that's also something I tend to downplay, as I don't like the NWO dominating three other Conventions by brainwashing all of their agents. Frankly, I don't see why Iteration X, the Progenitors, or the Syndicate would stand for it; and every bit as much as I dislike the \u201cliars or dupes\u201d interpretation of their view of the fundamentals, I also dislike portraying the Union as \u201cthe NWO and its lackeys\u201d \u2014 which is what you get if you put the NWO in charge of brainwashing everyone. In my games, the Void Engineers' \u201ccounter-Conditioning\u201d isn't as unique as it seems: <i>every</i> Convention (including the NWO) has similar programs in place to ensure that the NWO doesn't go too far, and/or has arranged to police its own, with what the \u201cConditioning\u201d section outlines being a standard that they pay lip service to (and sometimes even enforce) rather than being an iron-clad fact. <br /> <br /> And finally: while it doesn't excuse Conditioning by any means, the notion that there's some truth what they're indoctrinating does take an edge off of it. Let's take something that most of the readers here are likely to agree as being true: Climate Change. The Technocracy indoctrinates people (even their own) to believe in it. That's bad, because you're taking away peoples' free will \u2014 and even the Union understands that there's a time and place for it. But convincing people that it's true <i>without</i> some sort of Conditioning takes time, time that the Union doesn't always have. So they're willing to make some concessions on free will in the interest of pragmatism. But it doesn't make Climate Change any less true. <br /> <br /> More generally, that's my view on the Technocrats' basic doctrines: they <i>do</i> have a point (there are at least elements of reality that are objective, and building on them is better than ignoring then); but they don't always go about making their point in a good way. Just like the Traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-17-2020, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T19:41:22-07:00","id":1323587,"title":"","content":"Technocrats can\u2019t be liars because, in consensual reality, the people that control the consensus control the truth. This is where the discussion gets a little messy, because the difference between what technocrats do and \u201cmagic\u201d essentially depends on how the technocrats choose to define it. Traditions and Conventions operate in the same reality, but the conventions actively manipulate the consensus, rather than just trying to bend reality.<br /> <br /> Also, the N.W.O. lost the war for the minds of the other conventions, which is unfortunate given that they were fighting that war against outsiders. Unsurprisingly, the Void Engineers began having serious problems with outsider influence because of their constant encounters with aliens. They turned to the NWO for help and that worked for a while. ItX was corrupted through the chips they had (almost) all implanted in their brains that gave the computer influence over ItXers. The $yndicate was compromised by their close ties to Pentex as well as ItX and the Engineers. Interestingly, the avatar storm occurred not long after the NWO leadership finally fell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T21:19:58-07:00","id":1323605,"title":"","content":"I think, at least from my understanding they fall under the quote, from Arthur C. Clark, about how if technology gets significantly more advanced than what the audience understands it becomes indistinguishable from magic. Well the inverse is also true. Any magic once explained well enough becomes another form of science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T21:53:55-07:00","id":1323611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1323605#post1323605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, at least from my understanding they fall under the quote, from Arthur C. Clark, about how if technology gets significantly more advanced than what the audience understands it becomes indistinguishable from magic. Well the inverse is also true. Any magic once explained well enough becomes another form of science.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.girlgeniusonline.com/comic.php?date=20081205#.XSa-Vh5lB-E\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://www.girlgeniusonline.com/ggmain/strips/ggmain20081205b.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a>That would be an Etherite thing, mostly; in particular, it's Scientific Mysticism. It's not really something the Technocracy does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-11-2019, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T22:01:35-07:00","id":1323612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gothik_Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1323587#post1323587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technocrats can\u2019t be liars because, in consensual reality, the people that control the consensus control the truth. This is where the discussion gets a little messy, because the difference between what technocrats do and \u201cmagic\u201d essentially depends on how the technocrats choose to define it. Traditions and Conventions operate in the same reality, but the conventions actively manipulate the consensus, rather than just trying to bend reality.<br /> <br /> Also, the N.W.O. lost the war for the minds of the other conventions, which is unfortunate given that they were fighting that war against outsiders. Unsurprisingly, the Void Engineers began having serious problems with outsider influence because of their constant encounters with aliens. They turned to the NWO for help and that worked for a while. ItX was corrupted through the chips they had (almost) all implanted in their brains that gave the computer influence over ItXers. The $yndicate was compromised by their close ties to Pentex as well as ItX and the Engineers. Interestingly, the avatar storm occurred not long after the NWO leadership finally fell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got it. So you're arguing specifically from an NWO perspective \u2014 and a particularly extremist NWO perspective, at that. In that case, have fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T22:28:58-07:00","id":1323614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1323611#post1323611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <a href=\"http://www.girlgeniusonline.com/comic.php?date=20081205#.XSa-Vh5lB-E\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://www.girlgeniusonline.com/ggmain/strips/ggmain20081205b.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></div></div> </div> </div>That would be an Etherite thing, mostly; in particular, it's Scientific Mysticism. It's not really something the Technocracy does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah my mistake please forgive me the more I talk about this to people the more I make sense of it. Being proven wrong is never a bad thing, as long as you learn from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T09:03:13-07:00","id":1323700,"title":"","content":"I always believed the difference between Magick and Enlightened Science was relatively easy to thematically distinguish.<br /> From what I always interpreted, Technocratic Operatives basically saw their Enlightened Science as basically loopholes, backdoors, short cuts, and secret manipulations of both the laws of physics and reality. <br /> Essentially they were able to use thought to produce a reaction through incredibly complex and abstract scientific processes.<br /> Like with hurling lightning with their bare hands, ignoring how out of character it would be, of course. A Technomancer would see it as their Enlightened Mind is able to create certain reactions in their brains and bodies that basically cause a specific chain reaction with their hyperscientic theories, essentially using their own minds to create their Procedures.<br /> Like how you are always producing electromagnetic waves that change with your thoughts because your brain is moving bio-electricity. This incredibly subtle reaction then causes an increasingly powerful chain that builds up thanks to these &quot;occult physics&quot; and eventually that charge has built enough energy through Primal Energy that functions as the smallest building block of reality. They then hurl the lightning their altered brainwaves was able to, basically, calculate into existence.<br /> Even if an Operative isn't super smart, they have been taught how to actively trigger these reactions, and as such utilize these Procedures.<br /> When they are weaker they need tools and inventions to help activate those abstract laws of physics because the weight of Consensus prevents them from intuiting it all through their Genius. But at higher levels their Genius is able to more directly impact the Consensus by sheer power of its hyperscience.<br /> Think of it like how a shaman will use a certain herb to help heal sickness. They claim its a gift from the god created by his falling tears when he watched his mortal lover perish from sickness. Granting his lover's people a means to prevent what happened to them from happening again.<br /> The Technomancer would say that the herb simply has properties that trigger certain chemicals in the body that help increase immune system response, as well as stimulate the body's natural healing. No mumbo jumbo required, and if you know these properties you can use it more efficiently and for multiple things.<br /> I always assumed that was the differences between them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25226-knightfenrirwulfhart","name":"KnightFenrirWulfhart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T09:41:32-07:00","id":1323706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1323612#post1323612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Got it. So you're arguing specifically from an NWO perspective \u2014 and a particularly extremist NWO perspective, at that. In that case, have fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>No that\u2019s a generalist Technocracy perspective. The technocracy in general is all about manipulating the consensus. The Void Engineers have taken to mostly avoiding consensual reality by staying off planet and out of dimension, so they don\u2019t often run into this problem. I don\u2019t know how the progenitors really view consensus reality, but it should be pretty easy for them to explain why they can do things that others can\u2019t, since they have a large focus on making themselves better. ItX views consensus reality as a tool to be manipulated.. what we might consider to be a \u201clie\u201d, to them is required for the proper use of their tool. As I\u2019ve said before, the $yndicate generally controls consensus by controlling the masses and the NWO controls consensus by controlling the signal, but at least 3/5 of the technocracy is all about controlling consensus, and the other 2/5 is not likely to suffer from the problem we\u2019re discussing.<br /> <br /> Given the specific example that was previously mentioned (dropping a firearm, someone else picks it up and can\u2019t use it), The ItXer would almost certainly explain it as a smart chip or other safety feature. $yndicate would be unlikely to even have such a weapon, if they did, they would either be using a loaner from ItX which would have the same safety features, or they would use a NWO like rationale.<br /> <br /> I understand that the specific scenario doesn\u2019t address the whole of the question in the title, but a very generic question requires a very generic answer, that generic answer is that the difference between science and magic is what the consensus, and the people manipulating the consensus (not the NWO, but most of the technocracy) say it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T10:20:45-07:00","id":1323717,"title":"","content":"I'll have to disagree with you here. All of the Conventions acknowledge the Masses; but messing with the Consensus is primarily an NWO thing in much the same way that messing with Tychoidean Cosmology is a Void Engineer thing, or messing with Hypereconomics is a Syndicate thing. Each Convention has its own specialty; and while each acknowledges that the other specialties exist, they generally leave questions about them up to the experts in those fields. <br /> <br /> And this compartmentalized nature of the Technocratic \u201cparadigm\u201d means that the aforementioned acknowledgement of the other specialties is often no more than lip service. In practice, there isn't a unified Technocratic paradigm, but rather five interlocking paradigms. The idea that reality is shaped by the beliefs of the Masses is not something that any Convention other than the NWO truly believes beyond \u201cthe NWO says it's so, and that's their area of expertise; so I guess I'll roll with it\u201d. <br /> <br /> And even among the NWO, the idea that <i>physical</i> reality is shaped by the minds of the Masses is something of an outlier belief: they generally leave questions about how and why their gadgets and devices work to the Conventions that specialize in such matters, such as Iteration X. And Iteration X does <i>not</i> generally believe that machines work because the Masses believe in them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T17:29:12-07:00","id":1323810,"title":"","content":"From convention book $yndiacte (pg. 11): \u201cThe masses demanded a consensual reality. We supplied it to them, creating the Union to fulfill the longest service contract in history.\u201d<br /> <br /> The other conventions aren\u2019t dupes of the NWO. They\u2019re co-conspirators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T06:03:20-07:00","id":1323934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1323113#post1323113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Guide to the Technocracy says nothing of the sort. It says they don't believe they are mages and then explains why there is a difference between what they do and what mages do. It's an Ideological difference. Not a practical one. They know they warp reality. They just think they do it responsibily.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We clever Mage players know that what the Technocracy<br /> does is functionally magic. A trained Technocrat's<br /> Procedures are just magical workings using a scientific<br /> focus. Enlightenment is just a fancy word for Arete.<br /> However, 90 percent of the Technocrats don't know<br /> that! To the average agent on the street, it's all about<br /> science and training. ..i<br /> Remember, the whole idea of &quot;influencing reality&quot;<br /> and &quot;willworking&quot; is really only understood by the upper<br /> echelons of the Union, and they aren't talking.<br /> <br /> guide to the technocracy page 44","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T08:22:06-07:00","id":1323961,"title":"","content":"Wasn\u2019t the guide to the technocracy written before the avatar storm? Before the avatar storm, the technocracy had essentially been taken over by nephandi and, apart from a few heroic individuals, were almost entirely antagonists. In post Avatar Storm and original Technocracy wanted to stop magic from existing, because mages were abusing their power and harming the Masses. When outsiders started heavily influencing the Technocracy, they co-opted the goal of destroying magic, because magic could be a powerful weapon against the outsiders, which meant that the Technocracy leaders started trying to get rid of all magic, instead of just \u201cirresponsible use of magic\u201d. <br /> <br /> The stuff with \u201cmagic doesn\u2019t exist at all\u201d, as far as I know, is mostly corrupted Technocracy, who are antagonists. If you want protagonist Technocracy, your talking about non-corrupted technocrats. Non corrupted Technocrats essentially see the difference between traditions and conventions as, the former are irresponsible willworkers, and the latter are responsible willworkers.<br /> <br /> However, to say that the corrupted technocrat field agents were \u201cdupes\u201d May still be a little harsh. Most of them were re-educated, brainwashed, drugged, taken over by the computer or whatever while they were still neophytes and never really had a fighting chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T09:59:21-07:00","id":1323983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gothik_Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1323961#post1323961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn\u2019t the guide to the technocracy written before the avatar storm? Before the avatar storm, the technocracy had essentially been taken over by nephandi and, apart from a few heroic individuals, were almost entirely antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>the guide to the technocracy is what made technos into protagonists<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T10:50:33-07:00","id":1323999,"title":"","content":"Guide to the Technocracy was written right at the end of the 2e line; it was, if I remember correctly, the last book that Phil Brucato was involved in, and already showed the influence of the Revised Edition writers: MRev was already in development, so efforts were being made for GttTech to be compatible with it \u2014 including, if I recall correctly, some references to what MRev would call the Avatar Storm. So while it's technically a 2e supplement, it's one of three such supplements that could be treated as MRev supplements, too (the other two being Initiates of the Art and Masters of the Art). <br /> <br /> The notion that the Technocracy was infiltrated by the Nephandi is first stated clearly in M20; and even there, a point is made that the degree of infiltration is left entirely up to the Storyteller, with M20's now-famous \u201cthree routes\u201d approach. Yes, the original Convention Books were written primarily from the perspective of the Technocracy as antagonists, and included elements that in retrospect could maybe be attributed to Nephandic influence (though honestly, I think it's just as likely that ItX's Computer was Weaver-related and not the sort of thing the Nephandi would have been interested in pushing). But it's just as possible \u2014 and to me, more horrific \u2014 that the Technocracy did that to themselves. <br /> <br /> As well, the effort to portray Technocrats as potential protagonists started <i>long</i> before MRev: the first hint of it that I recall was way back in the 1e supplement, Book of Shadows, which included a vignette about an NWO agent going up against a Cultist of Ecstasy who was responsible for flooding the streets of the agent's \u201cbeat\u201d with drugs; that vignette was paired with text describing how to portray a Technocrat as a good guy. The point is that you don't need an Avatar Storm \u201csevering the head\u201d to reform the Technocracy \u2014 although I'll admit it helps. I mention that because M20 likewise leaves the question of whether or not there even was an Avatar Storm up to the Storyteller. You shouldn't be forced to invoke the Avatar Storm to portray the Union as a relatively sympathetic organization. <br /> <br /> Back to the topic at hand: I agree that the notion that \u201cMagick isn't real\u201d isn't a viable position to hold. As I stated early in this thread, a Technocrat who doesn't believe that Magick is real is in a state of Denial; and I'm perfectly fine with the notion that there may be a sizable population of Technocrats who <i>are</i> in Denial, as an unintended consequence of Conditioning (which, incidentally, is still very much a thing even in the Revised Convention Books). That said, I consider \u201cMagick doesn't exist\u201d to be a separate matter from \u201cEnlightened Science isn't Magick\u201d. And I believe it's possible to present the setting in such a way that the Technocracy believes the latter <i>and isn't necessarily wrong</i>. All you have to do is shift your mindset from \u201cthe Purple Paradigm is an ironclad truth of the game\u201d to \u201cthe Purple Paradigm is what the <i>Traditions</i> believe to be true\u201d. It becomes more of a \u201cBlind Men and the Elephant\u201d scenario, where both the Traditions and the Technocracy can point to evidence supporting their position; but <i>neither side</i> has it precisely right. <br /> <br /> With that approach, you don't need to resort to \u201cthe Technocracy was corrupted\u201d as an explanation for why so many of their Enlightened agents don't believe that they're doing magick, which is basically just a variation on the same theme of \u201cthey've been brainwashed and deceived\u201d: it just uses a slightly different explanation as to who has been doing the brainwashing. It's <i>still</i> essentially \u201cthe Traditions are fundamentally right; and until the Technocracy agrees with them, it will be fundamentally wrong\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-13-2019, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T18:53:26-07:00","id":1330183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1323934#post1323934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> We clever Mage players know that what the Technocracy<br /> does is functionally magic. A trained Technocrat's<br /> Procedures are just magical workings using a scientific<br /> focus. Enlightenment is just a fancy word for Arete.<br /> However, 90 percent of the Technocrats don't know<br /> that! To the average agent on the street, it's all about<br /> science and training. ..i<br /> Remember, the whole idea of &amp;quot;influencing reality&amp;quot;<br /> and &amp;quot;willworking&amp;quot; is really only understood by the upper<br /> echelons of the Union, and they aren't talking.<br /> <br /> guide to the technocracy page 44</div> </div> </div> </div>90% of the Technocracy is not made up of mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T21:23:53-07:00","id":1330203,"title":"","content":"I'm a big fan of Psychic Technocrats because it lets me play someone who does crazy science stuff but also lets me blow up heads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T21:54:32-07:00","id":1330206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1330183#post1330183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 90% of the Technocracy is not made up of mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that. And while I still say that there's more of a difference between the Traditions and the Technocracy than just a matter of ideology (I <i>don't</i> think even the Enlightened Scientists in their ranks buy into the notion that they're imposing their will in reality), I can definitely get behind the notion that 90% of the Union consists of Extraordinary Citizens or even just ordinary people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T22:44:41-07:00","id":1330212,"title":"","content":"I don't remember how numbery the Guide to Technocracy book gets but seeing as the Progenitors can just oven make agents, there's a lot of enlightened scientists.<br /> <br /> I know it says a majority of Men in Black are Clones and/or Enlighten Citizens just using Wonders/Perhaps doing Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> Someone did these stats &quot;<a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/eRVAoY5.png\" target=\"_blank\">http://i.imgur.com/eRVAoY5.png</a>&quot;<br /> <br /> It lists that sorcerers are super low in population compared to Mages, but the Technocracy seem to have a shit ton. Perhaps it doesn't include Enlightened Citizens under Sorcery even though the Sorcery book kinda/basically does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25315,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","user":"Jihelu","date":". 08-10-2019, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T02:13:53-07:00","id":1330508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1330212#post1330212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit:<br /> Someone did these stats &quot;<a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/eRVAoY5.png\" target=\"_blank\">http://i.imgur.com/eRVAoY5.png</a>&quot;<br /> <br /> It lists that sorcerers are super low in population compared to Mages, but the Technocracy seem to have a shit ton. Perhaps it doesn't include Enlightened Citizens under Sorcery even though the Sorcery book kinda/basically does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, careful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Those are stats done by our resident <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5307_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5307\" data-vbnamecard=\"5307\">loomer</a> who did a lot of demographics for oWoD in general, as well as Mage specifically in this thread: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038344-the-demographics-of-mage\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...aphics-of-mage</a><br /> He has a Database of a lot of book contents and builds up Statistics of characters, mentions etc.<br /> <br /> So if I recall right, what you see there regarding sorcerors are the *named* Sorcerors vs. *named* Mages. Best to check that thread.<br /> if in doubt, maybe we can get Loomer's attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-12-2019, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T08:12:58-07:00","id":1338276,"title":"","content":"I'm a little late here but in that case, it's not named but known and doesn't include the biggest single hit of Technocratic enlightened citizens as, per the intent of the book's author, the 12,000 of them on the New Cop are mostly mundane humans and not sorcerors at all. There are actually very few named sorcerors and most of the high figures are just 'pop figures' - references in books (usually the ones introducing the craft) to 200 total or whatever. It specifically doesn't include 'ratioed' populations (e.g., if we know that there are five sorcerors to every mage, the added population of &lt;x&gt; sorcerors is a 'ratioed' population - one with no other information available other than that it must exist to meet the description of the setting, which came up most prominently in the Changeling demographics due to the Concordian parliament and the massive overrepresentation of Sidhe in the source material).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T13:02:18-07:00","id":1338331,"title":"","content":"Huh, the demographics will be interesting to look at.<br /> <br /> Anyhow relating to the original discussion.... anyone ever spend any length of time amongst 'hard' science fiction fans*? If you have, you'll note that they often argue (violently) over what qualifies as real and 'magical'. And the notions of what is 'realistic' have changed over the decades as the fandoms have changed and you have all these little camps that have their own views about what is or isn't right.<br /> <br /> When you have a 'consensual reality' setting like WoD's MtA, it doesn't become hard to think that people's 'reality' of science might also differ.<br /> <br /> case in point being FTL neutrinos or the EM Drive over the last few years. I've seen TONS of argument over whether those are realistic or not. Or things like wormholes, or alcubierre drives, or so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> I've also seen some explanations of the underlying physics of a laser that are insanely realistic and quite plausibly near-future (given certain assumptions) as well.<br /> <br /> A variation of that would also be (from the mage perspective) how sorcerers, vampires, Werewolves and the like can all have 'static' magic that doesn't invoke paradox. Or psychic powers invoking paradox. They represent a specialized sort of 'consensual reality' in the same vein as UFO believers, ghost chasers, believers in psychic phenomena and fortunetellers, and the like (some of which were examples given in books like Sorcerer, IIRC.) Some sort of near-future hard-scifi nerd explanation for a pulse laser rifle would probably be the Technocratic Union equivalent of static magic.<br /> <br /> *I'll note I'm speaking as probably one of those math obsessed, technophillic nerd types, so this is somewhat self-referential. lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T22:38:36-07:00","id":1338401,"title":"","content":"I think saying 'All Technocrats should feel stupid they actually do magick ha!' is in the same realm of silly as people going &quot;Heh, my atheist friend said 'thanks' when I said 'bless you' when he sneezed, I knew he was a Christian in denial!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T07:01:57-07:00","id":1338620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1338401#post1338401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think saying 'All Technocrats should feel stupid they actually do magick ha!' is in the same realm of silly as people going &quot;Heh, my atheist friend said 'thanks' when I said 'bless you' when he sneezed, I knew he was a Christian in denial!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it's the other way arround.<br /> <br /> The atheist friend says thanks w/o accepting the implications (thanking the intention or because it's tradition, not because there's an actual blessing). No problem there, right?...<br /> <br /> ...well, <i>what if there was an actual, undeniable, physical blessing </i><i>that the atheist it's actively and consciously trying to gain by saying 'thanks'</i> (and therefore beliveves in it) while at the same time he denies any value to those Christian words?.<br /> <br /> In that case I think everyone would think the atheist it's being stupid or blind...unless he can give another, scientific (or at least not religious), explanation of why those words and only those words produce the &quot;blessing effect&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's where you need to step on to understand Technocrats. It's not that they're silly to call science what they do, Traditions are silly to call it magick (from their PoV, of course)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T10:33:03-07:00","id":1338648,"title":"","content":"Exactly. This thread is at the heart of my interpretation of Mage's metaphysics, and why I cannot accept the idea that the Purple Paradigm (that reality is fundamentally subjective, and that magick is enlightened will altering reality) is the absolute, incontrovertible Truth. <br /> <br /> It can and should be what the Traditions <i>believe</i>, and there should be enough supporting evidence for it that <i>they're</i> not being foolish when they accept it as true. But by the same token, the Technocracy needs to have an alternative to the Purple Paradigm with its own supporting evidence so that <i>their</i> worldview <i>also</i> isn't obviously foolish for ignoring a blatant Truth about reality. This wasn't so much of a concern in the early days of the game when the Traditions were the game's protagonists and the Technocracy existed solely as a monolithic oppressor for them to fight against; but the more the game has evolved, the more it has tried to make the Technocrats viable alternatives for the game's protagonists. And in that role, they can't be, as I tend to phrase it, all liars or dupes. <br /> <br /> So how do you set up a world in which two seemingly opposed views about the fundamental nature of reality can <i>both</i> potentially be true? Very carefully; you have to thread the needle. And the first thing that you have to do is to remove the notion that either of their views <i>is</i> absolutely true. In order for there to be the possibility that the Technocrats might be <i>right</i>, there must also be the possibility that the Traditions might be <i>wrong</i>. And vice versa. So the ultimate Truth of the nature of reality can't be known; it must still be up for debate, as much as both the Traditions and the Technocracy might think otherwise. <br /> <br /> Then you need to construct a worldview for the Technocracy that, while being opposed to the worldview of the Traditions, isn't brittle and overly simplistic and thus easily disproven. In particular, it shouldn't deny that what the Traditions do is possible; just that it's not what the Technocrats do, and that there are good reasons why not. To deny the evidence in front of your eyes would be insane. <br /> <br /> Which is where the innovation of dividing Quiet up into multiple types factors in: like it or not, there <i>are</i> Technocrats who hold a belief system that's incompatible with reality \u2014 the aforementioned liars and dupes from earlier editions. My take on them is first, that they're wearing metaphysical blinders \u2014 what MRev called Clarity and what M20 calls Denial \u2014 and second, that they're in the minority. A <i>loud</i> minority that gives the entire Union a bad reputation; but still a minority. <br /> <br /> This not only explains the earliest takes on the Technocracy's perspective, it also lets you use the Union in that way even in the modern, more enlightened interpretation: if you want a cabal of Traditionists to throw down against a construct of Unionists who unironically refer to them as superstitionists and don't believe that magick is real, just say that they've succumbed to Denial. Maybe even throw in a Negation Man or two into the mix just to make them a bit more dangerous. <br /> <br /> But again, that should be a minority view in the modern take on the Technocracy. The modern Technocrat should allow that magick is real, but it's not what Technocrats do. And if magick has benefits that Enlightened Science lacks, then the opposite should also be true. Fortunately, even by the rules as written, it is. Where Traditionalists can surpass their instruments, Technocrats can mass-produce Wonders. I like to supplement that with them also having an easier time instructing Extraordinary Citizens to use Adjustments, both because Extraordinary Citizens with a Technocratic mindset are more common than adepts with a Traditionalist mindset and because the Union has superior teaching techniques. This gives a practical reason, not just an ideological one, for the Union to prefer Enlightened Science. It also serves as a challenge to the Traditions' ecumenical notions such as We Are All Gods In Disguise, reinforcing the idea that they might be wrong. On the other hand, the fact that a Technocrat can become a Traditionist and vice versa challenges this notion that Enlightened Science and Awakened Magick are two different things. Both sides have ways of resolving the dilemmas posed to them; so the debate continues. <br /> <br /> So, what is this worldview that the Technocracy holds? At it's heart, it's that the key to what they do isn't Willpower; it's Enlightenment. There <i>are</i> objective laws that reality obeys; but they're complex, and have many edge cases. Enlightened Science involves identifying those edge cases and using their instruments to exploit them. In that way, Tech Holds All Answers. To the extent that Willpower matters, it's only in the sense that Science requires self-discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-11-2022, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T12:19:20-07:00","id":1338666,"title":"","content":"That there is the metaphysical cornerstone of this thread and how it relates to the concept of Paradigm in general. Every single Paradigm has to account for the possibility of every other, with caveats to validate itself. Even if a craft remains in complete isolation, they would still have to adapt their reality model if and when they encounter other crafts.<br /> That's why 1ed Technocracy lacked coherence with the setting, while revised and 20th are trying to correct that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","name":"El Barto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T13:33:32-07:00","id":1339690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>El Barto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1338666#post1338666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That there is the metaphysical cornerstone of this thread and how it relates to the concept of Paradigm in general. Every single Paradigm has to account for the possibility of every other, with caveats to validate itself. Even if a craft remains in complete isolation, they would still have to adapt their reality model if and when they encounter other crafts.<br /> That's why 1ed Technocracy lacked coherence with the setting, while revised and 20th are trying to correct that</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah so an example I like is the Psychic Technocrat who has a very convenient explanation for RDs they encounter.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh so you hocus and you pocus and suddenly the tree is on fire. You're just activating latent psychic abilities using a ridiculous and archaic crutch.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean it explains everything. It's all latent psionic powers being channeled through methods which make sense to the deviants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T19:48:05-07:00","id":1375737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1339690#post1339690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah so an example I like is the Psychic Technocrat who has a very convenient explanation for RDs they encounter.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh so you hocus and you pocus and suddenly the tree is on fire. You're just activating latent psychic abilities using a ridiculous and archaic crutch.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean it explains everything. It's all latent psionic powers being channeled through methods which make sense to the deviants.</div> </div> </div> </div>yep makes perfect sense. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T12:57:37-07:00","id":1375845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1338620#post1338620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think it's the other way arround.<br /> <br /> The atheist friend says thanks w/o accepting the implications (thanking the intention or because it's tradition, not because there's an actual blessing). No problem there, right?...<br /> <br /> ...well, <i>what if there was an actual, undeniable, physical blessing </i><i>that the atheist it's actively and consciously trying to gain by saying 'thanks'</i> (and therefore beliveves in it) while at the same time he denies any value to those Christian words?.<br /> <br /> In that case I think everyone would think the atheist it's being stupid or blind...unless he can give another, scientific (or at least not religious), explanation of why those words and only those words produce the &amp;quot;blessing effect&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> That's where you need to step on to understand Technocrats. It's not that they're silly to call science what they do, Traditions are silly to call it magick (from their PoV, of course)</div> </div> </div> </div>That is, I think the issue with this argument. The conflict between the Traditions and Technocrats isn't mappable to Traditions and Atheists.<br /> <br /> The Technocrats don't disbelieve they're altering reality or that reality can be altered.<br /> <br /> It's a conflict between Christian's and Satanists.<br /> <br /> Both believe in the same underlying framework. Reality is altered by belief and will. But they hold diametrically opposed beliefs on how you should respond to that.<br /> <br /> The traditions want to embrace the 'anything is possible' line, and just do whatever.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy wants to create a world with ordered rules so as to stave off a perceived inevitable annihilation of mankind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T15:44:32-07:00","id":1375869,"title":"","content":"I definitely agree that a key element is that the Traditions and Technocracy have diametrically opposed goals, with each seeing what the other doing as dangerous. But no, I don't think that they're on the same page as to what the underlying framework is. I mean, they <i>do</i> both agree that what the other side does gets results; you don't have many Technocrats who don't believe that magick is real, and the ones who don't are arguably in the throes of Denial. <br /> <br /> But no, I don't believe that the average Technocrat believes that what he himself does involves altering reality by belief and will; rather, the keys that the Technocrat possesses are enlightenment and discipline: knowledge of what <i>is</i> instead of belief in what one <i>wants</i>, and precise application of that knowledge rather than bending reality to your will. He'll even acknowledge that what a <i>mage</i> does involves imposing one's beliefs on reality by force of will \u2014 and that that's inherently dangerous and not the sort of thing that <i>he</i> would dabble in, thank you very much. <br /> <br /> And on both sides of the debate, it's not that every Focus needs to be able to explain what everyone else does in terms of their own beliefs or understanding; though that's a laudable goal if you can achieve it. It's more that they need only acknowledge that other ways also work, even if you personally find them unacceptable. A Verbena doesn't need to be able to explain what a Virtual Adept is doing in terms of her views about witchcraft; she need only accept that what the VA does <i>works</i>. More generally, your Focus need only explain what <i>you</i> do; there's no obligation for it to explain what <i>others</i> do. <br /> <br /> And frankly, thinking that you have to explain <i>everything</i> is a trap that <i>both</i> the Traditions and the Technocracy have fallen into, albeit in radically different and opposed ways. Frankly, this is arguably where the <i>Disparates</i> have a valid point, as they don't even <i>attempt</i> some Grand Unified Theory of Magick (or Science, for that matter).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-20-2020, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T20:06:24-07:00","id":1376059,"title":"","content":"Except the entire Technocratic structure disagrees with you. They go through monumental lengths to keep the masquerade entirely BECAUSE that let's them control the consensus. It was their meddling with the consensus on a monumental scale that gave them the upper hand to take their position of power to begin with.<br /> <br /> Everything they do implies that they not only understand that belief can shape the world, but relies upon that very fact as a cornerstone of their every strategy. If belief can shape the world, then they must control beliefs, with no deviation allowed to remain in existence.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if belief can change the world, beliefs become dangerous. You need to discipline your beliefs, shape them consistently, and when it becomes apparent that it's necessary, cast them aside.<br /> <br /> The last was the crime that caused the Etherites, and the Virtual Adepts to rebel. Both were too enamored with a belief that was dangerous. So when the Union commanded it's abandonment... They left.<br /> <br /> The only real mystical difference they outline in the guide to the Technocracy is the Technocrats lack of belief in the Avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T03:36:02-07:00","id":1376097,"title":"","content":"Arguably, the only Convention that concerns itself with what people believe is the New World Order; and they don't need to buy into \u201cbelief literally shapes reality\u201d to want to regulate it. It's enough that the universe of discourse that they focus on \u2014 the world of the mind \u2014 is by definition subject to the whims of belief. They are, after all, based off of such source material as 1984, which featured thought police without featuring the idea that reality itself can literally be controlled by such; you don't need the Metaphysics of Magick as stated by the Traditions for belief to be dangerous.<br /> <br /> Though again, key to my thesis is that the Conventions draw a line between \u201cwhat we (Enlightened Scientists) do\u201d and \u201cwhat they (the Superstitionists) do\u201d; and they're willing to admit that what the Traditions and others do features willfully imposing one's own beliefs on Reality. They just don't see their own feats in that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-22-2020, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T01:34:20-07:00","id":1376225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302901-how-to-explain-technocrats-not-knowing-some-of-their-effects-are-obviously-magical?p=1376059#post1376059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the entire Technocratic structure disagrees with you. They go through monumental lengths to keep the masquerade entirely BECAUSE that let's them control the consensus. It was their meddling with the consensus on a monumental scale that gave them the upper hand to take their position of power to begin with.<br /> <br /> Everything they do implies that they not only understand that belief can shape the world, but relies upon that very fact as a cornerstone of their every strategy. If belief can shape the world, then they must control beliefs, with no deviation allowed to remain in existence.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if belief can change the world, beliefs become dangerous. You need to discipline your beliefs, shape them consistently, and when it becomes apparent that it's necessary, cast them aside.<br /> <br /> The last was the crime that caused the Etherites, and the Virtual Adepts to rebel. Both were too enamored with a belief that was dangerous. So when the Union commanded it's abandonment... They left.<br /> <br /> The only real mystical difference they outline in the guide to the Technocracy is the Technocrats lack of belief in the Avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That same books explicitly says, in no uncertain terms, that almost all technocrats do now know they are doing magick. Other books confirm it. Both old and new.<br /> <br /> Maybe what you are describing would make much more sense, but it's just now how it is in canon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T10:13:13-07:00","id":1379014,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s my take on the matter: A Technocratic Enlightened Scientist doesn\u2019t \u201cbelieve in magick\u201d the same way most RL chemists don\u2019t \u201cbelieve in alchemy\u201d. Sure, the alchemist might know a few tricks like making napalm, but that doesn\u2019t mean his beliefs about how the process works are objectively correct. The Technocrat believes that the Superstitionists are using the same principles of Enlightened Science that he does, but are using them in dangerous and unpredictable ways due to their lack of proper understanding. A more philosophical Technocrat might concede that Enlightened Science hasn\u2019t discovered everything yet, and maybe, just MAYBE the so-called \u201cMages\u201d of the Traditions might know a few things they don\u2019t. Sifting through all the occult detritus to find those few nuggets of truth probably isn\u2019t worth the hassle, though. Easier to just brainwash\u2026 I mean, re-educate the poor misguided mystics instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> TLDR: Technocrats don\u2019t believe they\u2019re doing magick, and neither are other &quot;mages&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26077-chaotic-nipple","name":"Chaotic-nipple","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T11:29:17-07:00","id":1379025,"title":"","content":"It's also probably pertinent to remember that not every technocrat's going to be making laser guns or macgyvering super-machines, that mostly IT-X. Most Technocrats are just going to be using their enlightenment to empower their Existing mundane abilities.<br /> <br /> A technocratic super-scientist only really needs Mind 1(lower difficulty/add dice to mental rolls)for most of their Day-to-Day activities for instance. For most people, whether or not those procedures &quot;work&quot; for sleepers is going to be so immaterial that it'll be impossible to tell(even before using Human Resources as a focus).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}